{"shard": 12, "documents": [{"id": "1404", "title": "A Doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Top 5 Tips for Getting Through Cold and Flu Season", "url": "https://healthline.com/health/how-to-avoid-getting-sick", "final_url": "https://healthline.com/health/how-to-avoid-getting-sick", "text": "A family medicine physician shares simple, practical ways to stay healthier during cold and flu season and what to do if you start feeling sick.Cold and flu season can increase the risk of respiratory illnesses, including the common cold, influenza (the flu), and COVID-19. While there\u00e2\u0080\u0099s no guaranteed way to avoid getting sick, a few everyday habits may help lower your risk and reduce your chances of becoming seriously ill.Dr. Aaron Block (MD, MPH, CPH, DABFM, MSCP), a family medicine physician and co-founder and CEO of The Cove Concierge Medicine in Castle Rock, Colorado, says prevention often comes down to practical measures, such as vaccination, cleaner indoor air, handwashing, and supporting your overall health.Here are his top tips for staying healthy during the colder months. Use multiple strategies to lower your risk of getting sickOne of the most effective ways to protect yourself during respiratory virus season is to combine several preventive strategies rather than relying on just one.\u00e2\u0080\u009cWe learned a few things during the COVID-19 pandemic that are still useful for every respiratory virus season. My short list: get the immunizations recommended for you, improve the air you share with other people, wash your hands, and stay home when you are sick. A well-fitting mask adds protection in crowded indoor spaces, particularly if you or someone close to you is at higher risk.\u00e2\u0080\u009d \u00e2\u0080\u0094 Dr. Aaron BlockImprove indoor air quality. Respiratory viruses can spread through particles released into the air when people breathe, talk, cough, or sneeze. Opening windows when practical or using an air cleaner may help reduce indoor exposure.Wash your hands regularly. This is especially important after touching shared surfaces and before eating or touching your face. Dr. Block also recommends coughing or sneezing into a tissue or your elbow rather than your hands.Stay home when you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re sick. Limiting close contact with others can help reduce the chance of spreading a respiratory infection.Wear a well-fitting mask when it makes sense. Masks can add another layer of protection in crowded indoor spaces, particularly for people at higher risk of serious illness.Stay up to date on recommended vaccines. Ask your clinician which flu, COVID-19, respiratory syncytial virus (RSV), and pneumococcal vaccines are recommended for you based on your age, health conditions, and vaccination history. Vaccines can help reduce the risk of serious illness, although no vaccine can guarantee that you will not become sick.\u00e2\u0080\u009cThink of vaccination as a fire drill for your immune system: it gets to practice before the real alarm.\u00e2\u0080\u009d\u00e2\u0080\u0094 Dr. Aaron Block\u00c2\u00bbQUIZ:Can you debunk common cold and flu myths?Support your immune system with everyday habitsYou do not need a complicated wellness routine to support your immune system. Instead, focus on a few everyday habits you can realistically stick with, such as:getting enough sleepmoving your body regularlyeating a variety of nutritious foodsfinding ways to manage stressSleepSleep is a good place to start. In a 2026 study of 521 primary care patients, people with insomnia had roughly twice the odds of reporting an infection or flu-like illness at follow-up.As Dr. Block explains, the study does not prove that better sleep will prevent illness, \u00e2\u0080\u009cbut it gives us one more reason to take sleep seriously.\u00e2\u0080\u009dExerciseStaying active may help, too. Research suggests that people who are more physically active may have a lower risk of some infections. You do not need an intense workout routine to benefit. The goal is to move regularly in a way that works for you.Stress managementStress can also affect how your body responds to illness. Research has linked long-term stress with a greater chance of infection and a weaker response to some vaccines. Making time for rest, social support, or other stress-relieving activities may be one more way to support your overall health.NutritionWhat you eat matters as well. Aim for a variety of foods that provide protein, vitamins, minerals, and other nutrients your body needs.\u00e2\u0080\u009cProtein, fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and other nutrient-rich foods provide the raw materials your immune system needs; deficiencies can interfere with normal immune function.\u00e2\u0080\u009d\u00e2\u0080\u0094 Dr. Aaron Block\u00c2\u00bbMORE:15 foods that boost the immune systemBe selective about vitamins and supplementsThe supplement aisle can be particularly tempting during cold and flu season, but more is not necessarily better.\u00e2\u0080\u009cI would start with the least exciting answer: correct a real nutritional gap rather than buying a basket of products labeled \u00e2\u0080\u0098immune boosting,\u00e2\u0080\u0099\u00e2\u0080\u009d Dr. Block explains. \u00e2\u0080\u009cNo supplement replaces vaccination, sleep, or reducing exposure.\u00e2\u0080\u009d \u00e2\u0080\u0094 Dr. Aaron BlockVitamin CVitamin C is one example. Routine vitamin C supplementation does not appear to prevent colds in most people, although regular supplementation may modestly shorten the duration or reduce the severity of symptoms. Dr. Block recommends focusing on getting enough vitamin C from foods such as citrus fruits, bell peppers, strawberries, broccoli, and tomatoes. A supplement may be appropriate if you are not getting enough through your diet.Vitamin DVitamin D may be useful for people who are deficient, but Dr. Block says the evidence for taking it specifically to prevent respiratory infections is mixed.\u00e2\u0080\u009cIf deficiency is a concern, discuss testing or an appropriate dose with your clinician instead of assuming that more is better,\u00e2\u0080\u009d he says.Because vitamin D is fat-soluble, excessive amounts can accumulate in the body and may be harmful.ProbitiocsProbiotics have also been studied for the prevention of respiratory illness. Some research suggests they may reduce the incidence of certain upper respiratory infections, but results vary depending on the probiotic product and study.One reason they may help is that the gut plays an important role in immune function, and supporting a healthy balance of gut bacteria may help your immune system respond to germs.Eating a variety of fiber-rich foods, such as fruits, vegetables, whole grains, beans, and nuts, can help support the beneficial bacteria that live in your gut. Fermented foods, such as yogurt, kefir, kimchi, and sauerkraut, may also help support a healthy gut microbiome.ZincUnlike some supplements marketed for preventing illness, zinc may have a role after cold symptoms begin.Some research suggests that oral zinc, such as zinc lozenges, may shorten the length of a cold when started soon after symptoms appear. However, the evidence is not conclusive, and zinc can cause side effects such as nausea and an unpleasant taste.Dr. Block notes that research has not identified one zinc product or dose that is guaranteed to work. Avoid zinc products used inside the nose, which have been linked with long-lasting or permanent loss of smell.\u00c2\u00bbMORE:Editors share their cold and flu solutionsAct early if you start feeling sickIf you wake up with a scratchy throat, stuffy nose, cough, or body aches, you may not immediately know whether you have a cold, the flu, or COVID-19. For most otherwise healthy adults with mild symptoms, the first steps are fairly simple.Consider testing for flu or COVID-19Testing can help you figure out what is causing your symptoms and whether a specific treatment may be available. This is particularly important if you are at higher risk of developing serious illness.\u00e2\u0080\u009cIdentify what you might have, especially if you are at higher risk of complications,\u00e2\u0080\u009d Dr. Block says.\u00e2\u0080\u009cFlu antivirals work best when started within two days of symptoms, although treatment may still help some people who are very ill or at higher risk when started later. COVID-19 treatments for eligible people also have short start windows, generally within five to seven days, depending on the medication.\u00e2\u0080\u009dEven if you are generally healthy, knowing whether you have the flu, COVID-19, or a cold can help you make decisions about work, socializing, and exercise.Rest and drink plenty of fluidsFor a typical viral illness, there usually is not a quick fix. Give your body time to recover, get plenty of sleep and rest, and drink enough fluids to stay hydrated.\u00e2\u0080\u009cFor an ordinary cold, rest, fluids, and symptom relief are the mainstays. Antibiotics do not treat a viral cold,\u00e2\u0080\u009d Dr. Block says.Water, tea, broth, and other fluids can all help you stay hydrated. If you have a fever or are sweating more than usual, you may need to drink more than you typically would.Treat the symptoms that are bothering youOver-the-counter medications will not make a cold disappear, but they may make you more comfortable while you recover. Depending on your symptoms, options may include:acetaminophen or ibuprofen for fever, headaches, or body achessaline nasal spray for congestionthroat lozenges for a sore throathoney to soothe a coughA pharmacist or healthcare professional can help you choose an OTC medication, particularly if you take other medications or have an underlying health condition.Seek medical care if you have:trouble breathingsigns of severe dehydrationsevere or worsening symptomssymptoms that improve but then return or get worseKnow your risk factors for getting sick more oftenSome people may seem to catch every bug going around, but frequent illness does not necessarily mean their immune system is \u00e2\u0080\u009cweak.\u00e2\u0080\u009d\u00e2\u0080\u009cExposure is a huge part of the story. Living with children, working around many people, or caring for sick patients gives viruses more chances to find you.\u00e2\u0080\u009d \u00e2\u0080\u0094 Dr. Aaron BlockIn other words, getting sick often may simply reflect how frequently you come into contact with viruses.Other factors can affect how your body responds once you do get sick. Age, pregnancy, some chronic health conditions, and medications or treatments that suppress the immune system can increase the risk of more serious illness.The most important thing to pay attention to is not just how often you get sick, but what those illnesses are like for you.\u00e2\u0080\u009cIf someone has unusually frequent, severe, or hard-to-clear infections, that deserves a conversation with their clinician rather than another bottle of supplements,\u00e2\u0080\u009d Dr. Block says.If you regularly have infections that are unusually severe, last much longer than expected, or keep coming back, a healthcare professional can help determine whether there is an underlying reason.\u00c2\u00bbMORE:Why do I keep getting sick?TakeawayAvoiding every cold, flu, or COVID-19 infection may not be realistic, but you can take steps to lower your risk and protect your health. Staying current on recommended vaccines, improving indoor air, washing your hands, getting enough sleep, eating a varied diet, staying active, and giving yourself time to rest when you are sick can all be part of a practical prevention plan. If symptoms do develop, identifying the illness early may also help you access treatments for the flu or COVID-19 within the window when they are most useful.", "content_hash": "a46d843c86f37a85f9648fc7e1234db31e4ad611f1073ec2fe588c5cd4e774ee", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:37.691954+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1405", "title": "Sale of Chattels of Closed Primary Mortgage Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid.", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=sale-of-chattels-of-closed-primary-mortgage-banks-by-public-auction-and-public-competitive-bid", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=sale-of-chattels-of-closed-primary-mortgage-banks-by-public-auction-and-public-competitive-bid", "text": "Sale of Chattels of Closed Primary Mortgage Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid. N NDIC June 15, 2026 4 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), in exercise of its right as Liquidator of failed Primary Mortgage Banks (PMBs), hereby invites interested members of the general public to buy the assets (furniture, fixture, fittings, equipment, generators, motor vehicles etc) of the under listed defunct PMBs by PUBLIC COMPETITIVE SEALED BIDDING/AUCTION.UNION HOMES SAVINGS & LOANS(Auction Dates: 23/06/2026 \u2013 25/06/2026)Rivers State4 Godis Close, off Power Encounter Road, Ellowanhi, off East-West Road, Port-HarcourtAuctioneer: Beautiful Feathers Global LTDNDIC Contact: PORT HARCOURT ZONAL OFFICE, No. 104, Woji Road, off Olu Obasanjo Road, GRA, Port Harcourt \u2014 08023202134Delta StatePlot 146, Okpanam Road, AsabaAuctioneer: Sheyi Oladeji (08121120547)NDIC Contact: BENIN ZONAL OFFICE, No. 28A & B, Benoni Road, Off Airport Road, GRA, Benin City, Edo State \u2014 08035727023FCT, AbujaPlot 1479, 12 Ago Oro Crescent, off Ahmadu Bello Way, GarkiAuctioneer: Arinze Nnochukwu & Associates (08033110393)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798Kaduna StateV20 Ahmadu Bello Way, Zaria Road, KadunaAuctioneer: Abdulhad Logistics LTD (08033085931)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798Kano State37, Niger/Murtala Mohammed Way, Kano (Chattels moved to NDIC Kano Office)Auctioneer: Kunle Amao & Co (08060349049)NDIC Contact: KANO ZONAL OFFICE, Plot 44/45, Muhammad Muhammad Avenue, Off Maiduguri Road, Hotoro, G.R.A., Kano \u2014 07088877887ASO SAVINGS & LOANS(Auction Dates: 23/06/2026 \u2013 25/06/2026)FCT, AbujaCorporate Head Office & Branch Office, Plot 266 FMBN Building, Central Area AbujaAuctioneer: Abu Usman Consulting (08036101758)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798Parking Lot, Opp. Federal Secretariat Building, Eagle Square, AbujaAuctioneer: Arinze Unochuckwu & Associates (08033110398)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798Three Arms Zone, National Assembly, AbujaAuctioneer: Sina Adiatud & Co (08034044331)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798Closing Bwari Branch (Bank's Archive), No. 1 Lafia Close Area 8 GarkiAuctioneer: Sina Adiatu & Co (08034044331)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798Kaduna28 Imam House, Ahmadu Bello Way, KadunaAuctioneer: Abdulhad Logistics LTD (08033085931)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798LagosNo. 19 Oba Akran Way, IkejaAuctioneer: Kene Onuora ConsultingNDIC Contact: NDIC (ASSET MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT) \u2014 Garba 08062616662, John 08029997846, Aliyu 08062657895No. 18 Construction House, Adeyemo Alakija Street, Victoria IslandAuctioneer: Alao & Co (08062512654)NDIC Contact: NDIC (ASSET MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT) \u2014 Garba 08062616662, John 08029997846, Aliyu 08062657895OndoTisco House, Alagbaka, AkureAuctioneer: Patron Auctioneers Nigeria LTDNDIC Contact: NDIC (ASSET MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT) \u2014 Garba 08062616662, John 08029997846, Aliyu 08062657895EdoNo. 38 Sapele Road, Benin CityAuctioneer: Kene Onuora ConsultingNDIC Contact: BENIN ZONAL OFFICE, No. 28A & B, Benoni Road, Off Airport Road, GRA, Benin City, Edo State \u2014 08035727023RiversNo. 2 Chona Street D/Line, Port HarcourtAuctioneer: Mamud Momodu & Associates (09034161701)NDIC Contact: PORT HARCOURT ZONAL OFFICE, No. 104, Woji Road, off Olu Obasanjo Road, GRA, Port Harcourt, Rivers State \u2014 08023202134AUCTION PROCESSThe Public Auction for the furniture, fixtures, fittings & equipment, etc (ASSETS) will take place from 23rd to 25th June, 2026. CONDITIONS FOR BIDDING FOR THE ASSETS1)Bids should be submitted in a sealed envelope together with a deposit of 10% of the bid price in Certified Bank Draft in favour of the respective primary mortgage banks (In-Liquidation) and with an inscription \u201cBID FOR ASSETS,\u201d on the top left hand corner of the envelope. The bid should contain the name, address and telephone numbers of the bidder. The successful bidder will be required to pay the balance of the bid price within 24 hours of winning the bid.2) Financial Institutions will be given preference.3)The 10% draft for the unsuccessful bidders would be returned immediately.4)Bids should be submitted to the Auctioneers or NDIC Contact persons within the stated period.5)Submitted bids shall be opened before the bidders at the various locations.6)All Assets are sold as \u201cas is\u201d and \u201cnet of all taxes\u201d.7)All purchased items must be evacuated within 24 hours of purchase. For further enquiries, please contact:Director, Asset Management Department,Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation, Lagos Office,Mamman Kotangora House (9th Floor),23A, Marina,Lagos.Tel No: 08035925533Lagos Office All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "1fe4537a9b1dc84ca6ba54638aaab9458df8365b484e26ab404f1106da1c2e14", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:38.646498+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1406", "title": "Cutting Back on Ultra-Processed Foods May Help Ease Depression Symptoms", "url": "https://healthline.com/health-news/cutting-back-ultra-processed-foods-may-help-depression-symptoms", "final_url": "https://healthline.com/health-news/cutting-back-ultra-processed-foods-may-help-depression-symptoms", "text": "Share on PinterestRecent research has found that reducing UPF intake may help improve symptoms of depression. cafotodigital \u00c2\u00b7 E+/GettyA small study found that reducing ultra-processed food (UPF) intake was associated with improvements in depression symptoms.The findings add to previous research linking high UPF consumption with an increased risk of depression.Researchers are investigating how factors such as nutrition, inflammation, metabolic health, and the gut-brain axis may link UPFs with mood.Emerging research has linked high consumption of ultra-processed foods (UPFs) with an increased risk of depression. Now, a small study published September 23 in JAMA Psychiatrysuggests that reducing UPF intake may help ease depression symptoms.There is no universally accepted definition of UPFs. However, a widely used classification system known as NOVA defines them as industrial formulations made primarily from substances extracted or derived from foods, often with additives not typically used in home cooking. Examples include soft drinks, packaged snacks, candy, sausages, hot dogs, and pastries. Previous research has linked UPFs to an increased risk of depression, anxiety, eating disorders, and other mental health conditions. In the new study, participants reduced their UPF intake by more than 85% and had significantly lower depression scores across three standard measures while following the low-UPF diet.Lowering ultra-processed food intake may improve depressionThis small study included 20 participants who:were between 18 and 80 years old had a primary diagnosis of depressionhad a Patient Health Questionnaire-9 (PHQ-9) score of at least 5consumed high amounts of UPFshad at least one self-reported metabolic abnormality, such as overweight or obesity, high blood pressure, high cholesterol or triglycerides, or insulin resistanceThe participants also had to agree not to change medications, therapy, exercise, or sleep during the study. Of the 20 participants enrolled in the study, 19 completed it. The average age was 44. Participants followed both their usual diet and a low-UPF diet during separate phases of the study, with the order randomly assigned.Participants generally found the low-UPF diet acceptable and manageable. They also had lower depression and anxiety scores during the low-UPF diet phase compared with their usual diet.On one commonly used depression measure, the PHQ-9, average scores declined from 8.68 during the usual diet phase to 5.53 during the low-UPF phase. The study had several limitations, including its small sample size, reliance on self-reported dietary data, and uncertainty about which aspects of reducing UPFs may have contributed to the changes in symptoms.The researchers also said that larger studies are needed to determine whether reducing UPF intake can improve depression symptoms.Michelle Routhenstein, Preventive Cardiology Dietitian at Entirely Nourished, who wasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t involved in the study, agreed, noting that more research is needed to understand whether reducing UPFs directly improves depression symptoms or whether other aspects of the overall diet may be contributing to the observed benefit.Dara Houp, PsyD, a licensed clinical psychologist with Pathways Psychological Services in NYC, who wasn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t involved in the study, told Healthline that it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to distinguish ultra-processed foods from processed foods more broadly.Routhenstein agreed that the distinction is important. \u00e2\u0080\u009cProcessing is not inherently negative. Many nutritious foods are processed in some way.\u00e2\u0080\u009d \u00e2\u0080\u009cI would not encourage people to simply label a food as \u00e2\u0080\u0098processed\u00e2\u0080\u0099 or \u00e2\u0080\u0098unprocessed\u00e2\u0080\u0099 and make decisions based on that label alone. I prefer to look at the overall dietary pattern, the nutritional value of the food, and what role that food plays in the diet. A packaged food can still provide meaningful nutrients and be part of an overall nutritious eating pattern,\u00e2\u0080\u009d she said. How can ultra-processed foods affect your mood?There are various proposed mechanisms for how UPFs may affect mood.For example, UPFs are often low in fiber, vitamins, and minerals, which can play important roles in brain health.Houp noted that some ingredients found in UPFs, including artificial sweeteners such as aspartame, may affect the gut microbiome.\u00e2\u0080\u009cOur gut is a primary location for producing neurotransmitters, responsible for manufacturing the vast majority \u00e2\u0080\u0093 upward of 90% \u00e2\u0080\u0093 of our body\u00e2\u0080\u0099s serotonin. When the gut microbiome is disrupted, it directly interferes with healthy neurotransmitter production,\u00e2\u0080\u009d she said. Houp added that diets high in UPFs may be lower in antioxidant-rich foods, such as fruits and vegetables, which could contribute to oxidative stress. Research suggests that people with depression may have lower antioxidant levels and higher markers of oxidative damage.Routhenstein also noted that researchers are investigating how UPF consumption may influence inflammation, metabolic health, and the gut-brain axis, all of which may have implications for mood.What are ways to reduce ultra-processed food intake?Reducing your UPF intake can start with small, sustainable changes.Routhenstein suggested starting by looking at the foods you eat most often rather than trying to overhaul your kitchen.\u00e2\u0080\u009cIdentify one or two foods that are frequent sources of UPFs and consider what you could realistically replace them with. For example, you might swap a daily sugary drink for water or sparkling water, or choose fruit, nuts, yogurt, or another minimally processed option in place of a packaged snack,\u00e2\u0080\u009d she said. Other ways you can help reduce UPFs include: Cook at home, using whole ingredients when possible.When possible, choose foods with fewer highly processed ingredients.Build meals around whole foods, like fruits, vegetables, grains, and lean proteins.Routhenstein added that you don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t have to eliminate convenience from your diet. Frozen vegetables, canned beans, canned fish, oats, plain yogurt, tofu, and other minimally processed foods can make healthy eating much more practical.\u00e2\u0080\u009cThe goal is not to eat a perfectly unprocessed diet. It is to gradually shift the overall pattern toward more nutrient-dense foods that provide fiber, protein, healthy fats, vitamins, and minerals,\u00e2\u0080\u009d she said.", "content_hash": "124d2ec5a106f87c3fb25b6093fed3e2fd8204d2e4c8cae613cb1d3988966840", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:40.268280+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1407", "title": "NDIC and NCGC Partner to Strengthen Banking System Resilience Through Unified Risk Management", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-and-ncgc-partner-to-strengthen-banking-system-resilience-through-unified-risk-management", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-and-ncgc-partner-to-strengthen-banking-system-resilience-through-unified-risk-management", "text": "NDIC and NCGC Partner to Strengthen Banking System Resilience Through Unified Risk Management The Executive Managements of the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) and the National Credit Guarantee Company (NCGC) are collaborating to deepen sound risk management and early warning systems in the financial services industry. N NDIC May 29, 2026 1 min read The Executive Managements of the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) and the National Credit Guarantee Company (NCGC) are collaborating to deepen sound risk management and early warning systems in the financial services industry.The partnership was formalized during a courtesy visit by NCGC's MD/CEO, Mr. Bonaventure Okhaimo, and his management team to NDIC's MD/CE, Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday in Abuja. Discussions centered on strengthening frameworks for banking sector resilience.The NCGC focuses on unlocking access to credit through risk-sharing mechanisms that support businesses and individuals. Conversely, the NDIC is committed to safeguarding depositors' funds and promoting confidence in the banking system, thereby strengthening financial intermediation and supporting inclusive economic development.The two Chief Executives agreed to leverage their complementary mandates to promote Unified Risk Management and Early Warning Systems. This coordinated approach aims to reinforce the resilience of the banking system while expanding access to credit for businesses and individuals.The partnership addresses a critical need: early identification of emerging risks enables timely intervention, preventing potential systemic threats. By combining the NCGC's credit risk expertise with the NDIC's depositor protection mechanisms, both institutions can create a more robust financial safety net.This collaborative framework demonstrates Nigeria's commitment to building a resilient financial system capable of supporting sustainable economic growth. The partnership's success depends on continuous information sharing, joint monitoring of industry trends, and coordinated policy responses to emerging challenges in the financial services sector. All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "58ea228e6be5eedaa04d44c3f5bd1461f3d266bb2089f0959bf58a2ca556c25f", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:41.553180+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1408", "title": "Letter From the Editor-in-Chief: Is Worrying About Sleep Keeping Us Awake?", "url": "https://healthline.com/health-news/sleep-study-parenthood-letter-from-eic-column", "final_url": "https://healthline.com/health-news/sleep-study-parenthood-letter-from-eic-column", "text": "Share on PinterestA recent study found that a lack of REM and deep sleep is linked to higher risks of dozens of diseases. Credit: GettyA new study analyzing wrist tracker data from 95,000 people found that higher amounts of REM and deep sleep were linked to a lower risk of 83 diseases combined, including dementia, hypertension, and Parkinson\u00e2\u0080\u0099s.Nearly 70% of Americans say anxiety disrupts their sleep \u00e2\u0080\u0093 and for some, the sleep trackers meant to help may be making it worse, a phenomenon researchers call orthosomnia.Healthline\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Editor-in-Chief Robin Hough shares why he\u00e2\u0080\u0099s taking the data, leaving the anxiety, and still setting his alarm for a very insistent 8-year-old.As a busy, sleep-deprived, middle-aged father of two young kids, including an irrepressible 8 year old ball of energy who is, without fail, up and ready to take on the world at 6 o\u00e2\u0080\u0099clock every morning (usually with a steady stream of questions about dinosaurs, the natural world and the origins of the universe in his back pocket), do I really need another set of headlines informing me that not only am I falling short in getting the requisite 40 winks a night but I\u00e2\u0080\u0099m also at risk of 83 diseases into the bargain? Apparently, I do. Another day, another headline-grabbing sleep study lands, this time linking a greater amount of sleep \u00e2\u0080\u0093 specifically sleep of the rapid eye movement (REM) variety, also known as dream sleep \u00e2\u0080\u0093 to a lower risk of dozens of diseases.What a 95,000-Person Study Reveals About SleepThe recent study published in PLOS Medicine found that REM sleep is linked to a lower risk of 83 diseases, including dementia, Parkinson\u00e2\u0080\u0099s, and multiple sclerosis (MS). As an added bonus, the study also found that a higher amount of deep sleep was associated with a lower risk of seven health conditions, including depression and type 2 diabetes. So far, so alarming for a self-confessed \u00e2\u0080\u009cbad sleeper\u00e2\u0080\u009d. Yet also fairly unsurprising. The accepted science, combined with anecdotal experience, has long told us that the right amount of good quality sleep corresponds directly with improved short and long-term health outcomes, both mental and physical. Evidence suggests that 7-9 hours of sleep per night is typically the sweet spot for a healthier life. Where this particular study differs from those that have come before is that scientists used wrist trackers to gather much more detailed information over a multi-year timeline about participants\u00e2\u0080\u0099 sleep stages, including irregular sleep patterns and variations in sleep duration. The findings were drawn from real-world data from more than 95,000 participants in the UK Biobank database.Orthosomnia: When Tracking Your Sleep Causes AnxietyNow, as the aforementioned and self-proclaimed VBP (very busy person \u00e2\u0080\u0093 if you know, you know), who works long hours across UK and US timezones for the day job whilst serving as a sub-par encyclopedia for the real boss (the aforementioned 8 year old) outside of work, the general demands and pressures of daily life are more than sufficient to make consistently good sleep something that is all too often out of reach. I know this to be true because the wearable I use reminds me of the fact with cold, hard data on a daily, if not hourly, basis. One of the first things my wife and I do each morning (after fending off existential questions from a third grader) is hawkishly plug into our Oura app to trade sleep scores and discuss what did or didn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t contribute to our invariably bad or, very rarely, good night\u00e2\u0080\u0099s sleep. Deep sleep, REM sleep, resting heart rate, heart rate variability, latency, even sleep debt \u00e2\u0080\u0093 a laundry list of data points that we pore over in a futile attempt to make our sleep consistency optimal whilst living a life that doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t readily allow for it. Scientists have even given this phenomenon a name \u00e2\u0080\u0093 Orthosomnia \u00e2\u0080\u0093 where the anxiety of analyzing and perfecting sleep scores actually disrupts rest and intensifies poor sleep, and in the most extreme cases, insomnia.It turns out we\u00e2\u0080\u0099re not alone. Results of a Gallup poll from 2024 \u00e2\u0080\u0093 with the rather on-the-nose headline \u00e2\u0080\u009cAmericans sleeping less, more stressed\u00e2\u0080\u009d \u00e2\u0080\u0093 showed Americans report averaging 6.5 hours of sleep per night, comfortably below the recommended baseline of 7+ hours. Perhaps more tellingly, in a survey from 2024, the American Academy of Sleep Medicine found that nearly 70% of Americans report losing sleep due to anxiety.Which brings me back to my original point. Anxiety-induced stress makes for the perfect bedfellow (pun intended) for a bad night\u00e2\u0080\u0099s sleep. The kind of anxiety-induced stress that can be both caused and amplified by obsessing over wearables data and a steady torrent of sleep-related content that aims to scaremonger rather than inform. Why Empathy Matters in Health Information \u00e2\u0080\u0093 and in Sleep In fairness to the UK Biobank study, it is unequivocally important and unique research steeped in actionable real-world data and peer-reviewed medical science. And yet we live in a world increasingly awash with AI-generated content, sporting sensationalist headlines and powered by algorithms designed with an inherent imbalance to engage rather than empower. In that environment, gold-standard scientific work like this is all too often reduced to the lowest common denominator. If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll indulge a minor tooting of our own horn here, this is precisely the inverse of how the team of wonderfully talented editorial misfits at Healthline Media thinks about and creates health information. We take research-backed science and our embedded clinical rigor and apply it to every aspect of our work. But we never lose sight of the fact that behind every study, there\u00e2\u0080\u0099s someone lying awake in the early hours running the math on their own risk factors, and that what they need in that moment is recognition that we are all at different stages on that journey, and a helping hand along the path to better health. Life isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t linear, sleep isn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t linear, and health is certainly not linear. Some nights I\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll get my seven hours. Plenty of others I won\u00e2\u0080\u0099t. And that is ok. Because either way, my alarm clock has a favorite dinosaur and a nonnegotiable 6 a.m. start time, and no peer-reviewed study or scary headline is going to change that. So I\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll take the data and the empathy, leave the anxiety, and see you all again at dawn.If there\u00e2\u0080\u0099s something keeping you awake at night, or you just want to learn more about the wonderful world of sleep, we have a wealth of science-backed information at our dedicated Sleep Health hub. There you can also find Healthline\u00e2\u0080\u0099s Better Sleep Challenge \u00e2\u0080\u0093 a three-week series designed to help you sleep better, feel more rested, and wake up ready to thrive each day.Robin Hough is the Editor-in-Chief of Healthline, and in addition to this regular Letter from the Editor column, he can be found every other Saturday in our Healthline Daily newsletter. He\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll soon be launching a dedicated Letter from the Editor newsletter coming to an inbox near you later in the fall.", "content_hash": "e6ead7fc81e672a1546426048ec972fe808513aa58205a9023333db72f1c8c42", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:43.019890+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1409", "title": "NDIC Reiterates Commitment to Enhance Financial System Stability", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-reiterates-commitment-to-strong-deposit-insurance-funding-to-enhance-financial-system-stability", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-reiterates-commitment-to-strong-deposit-insurance-funding-to-enhance-financial-system-stability", "text": "NDIC Reiterates Commitment to Enhance Financial System Stability The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) has reaffirmed its commitment to continuously strengthening its Deposit Insurance Funds (DIFs) N NDIC May 25, 2026 2 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) has reaffirmed its commitment to continuously strengthening its Deposit Insurance Funds (DIFs) as part of efforts to promote the stability and resilience of the nation\u2019s financial system.The Managing Director/Chief Executive of the Corporation, Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, stated this during a courtesy visit to the Director-General of the Budget Office of the Federation, Mr. Tanimu Yakubu, in Abuja.Mr. Sunday explained that the need to build strong Deposit Insurance Funds is critical to enhancing the Corporation\u2019s capacity to respond effectively to potential systemic crises in the banking sector without relying on government intervention.He noted that while financial crises may be inevitable, the NDIC has consistently prioritised robust DIFs as a key component of its contingency planning and crisis preparedness framework. According to him, this strategic approach enabled the Corporation to commence payments to depositors of Aso Savings & Loans and Union Savings & Loans within 72 hours following the revocation of their operating licences by the Central Bank of Nigeria in December 2025.The NDIC Boss further stated that the Corporation would continue to strengthen institutional collaboration with the Budget Office of the Federation and align its operations with the national budgetary framework. He added that the NDIC remains committed to working closely with the Budget Office to promote evidence-based planning and enhance its contributions to national economic growth and development.Mr. Sunday also underscored the importance of the Federal Government\u2019s vision of building a one-trillion-dollar economy by 2030, assuring that the NDIC would continue to play a significant role in supporting the realization of that goal.In his remarks, the Director-General of the Budget Office of the Federation, Mr. Tanimu Yakubu, commended the NDIC for its transparency in managing the Deposit Insurance Funds.He urged the Corporation to leverage technology-driven investment strategies to further strengthen the funds for the protection of depositors in the event of bank failures and to sustain public confidence in the financial system. He also encouraged the NDIC to benchmark its investment instruments against global best practices adopted by other deposit insurance institutions to further consolidate its funding framework.Hawwau GamboHead, Communication & Public Affairs Department All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "31fe294077947d26654df84c5d4cd6df54af9878ba2fac5ba6c0ff860d39c36d", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:43.590582+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1410", "title": "Can the BPC-157 \u00e2\u0080\u0098Wolverine\u00e2\u0080\u0099 Peptide Really Help With Pain and Recovery?", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health-news/bpc-157-wolverine-peptide-help-pain-recovery", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health-news/bpc-157-wolverine-peptide-help-pain-recovery", "text": "Share on PinterestA new study shows a 33-fold increase in new BPC-157 users in recent years. Compassionate Eye Foundation/Jonathan Bielaski/DigitalVision/Getty ImagesProponents of BPC-157, the \u00e2\u0080\u009cWolverine\u00e2\u0080\u009d peptide, tout injury recovery and pain relief despite limited human evidence to establish safety and effectiveness.Until the potential for adverse reactions is better understood, particularly with long-term use, experts advise against unapproved peptides.There are other proven treatment options for pain relief and recovery recommended by medical professionals.Wellness seekers are increasingly turning to BPC-157, the wildly popular \u00e2\u0080\u009cWolverine\u00e2\u0080\u009d peptide for injury recovery and pain relief, despite scant human evidence.The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) advisory panel voted in July to ease restrictions on it and several other peptides, recommending the injectable substances be made eligible for pharmacy compounding.But before restrictions were eased, preliminary research suggests a rise in the use of the Wolverine peptide in recent years.A September 2026 preprint analyzed more than 15 million medical records and identified 1,039 people with documented BPC-157 use. The researchers found a roughly 33-fold increase in new users between 2020 and 2026. The results, which were based on clinical records, have not yet been published in a peer-reviewed scientific journal.\u00e2\u0080\u009cThe study found that BPC-157 use is largely hidden in clinical narrative rather than conventional prescription data,\u00e2\u0080\u009d said lead study author Venky Soundararajan, PhD, co-founder and Chief Scientific Officer of nference.\u00e2\u0080\u009cThe proportion of newly documented BPC-157 users who were male rose from 57% in 2020 to 70% in 2026, a statistically significant trend,\u00e2\u0080\u009d he told Healthline. \u00e2\u0080\u009cThe user population for BPC-157 peptide is increasingly male in proportion and increasingly younger with each passing year.\u00e2\u0080\u009dWhat is BPC-157, and why is it so popular?BPC-157 is a synthetic 15-amino-acid peptide marketed and sold online for wellness. Health claims about it and other peptides have spread on social media and in fitness circles and wellness communities, with high-profile advocates like Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. touting their benefits.Proponents of BPC-157 claim the injectable peptide promotes injury recovery, pain relief, and tissue healing. Some advocates claim that \u00e2\u0080\u009cstacking\u00e2\u0080\u009d the Wolverine peptide, particularly with TB-500, may enhance its effects.The \u00e2\u0080\u009cWolverine\u00e2\u0080\u009d peptide got its nickname from claims that it facilitates rapid healing, echoing the regenerative abilities of the fictional X-Men character of the same name.This promise of pain relief and recovery may be what gives the Wolverine peptide its appeal.Soundararajan\u00e2\u0080\u0099s study found that nearly 33% of patients reported using BPC-157 for pain relief. By comparison, just 4% of patients reported using BPC-157 for performance enhancement. Across the cohort of 1,039 patients, 27% reported improvements. \u00e2\u0080\u009cPain relief was the dominant reported benefit, documented in 183 patients,\u00e2\u0080\u009d Soundarajan said. \u00e2\u0080\u009cWound or tissue healing was reported in 38 patients and functional return in 34 patients.\u00e2\u0080\u009d\u00e2\u0080\u009cPart of BPC-157\u00e2\u0080\u0099s appeal appears to be to patients who remain symptomatic after chronic, complex or previously treated musculoskeletal problems, signaling a clear clinical unmet need,\u00e2\u0080\u009d he said.Bert Mandelbaum, MD, a sports medicine specialist, orthopedic surgeon, and co-director of the Regenerative Orthobiologic Center at Cedars-Sinai Orthopaedics and Sports Medicine in Los Angeles, said that everyone experiences pain, but warned about the risks of using the Wolverine peptide to treat it.\u00e2\u0080\u009cThere is zero indication that BPC-157 has any efficacy for pain,\u00e2\u0080\u009d he told Healthline. \u00e2\u0080\u009cThere\u00e2\u0080\u0099s zero evidence that shows that it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s good for clinical healing, and we don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t really understand the safety profile of it.\u00e2\u0080\u009dWhat does the research say about BPC-157?Human evidence of the possible benefits and safety of the Wolverine peptide is limited. A 2025 systematic review of current BPC-157 literature found that it was dominated by preclinical research and low-grade human evidence. The review authors said there was insufficient clinical safety data to determine the peptide\u00e2\u0080\u0099s risks. A small 2021 retrospective study on the effects of injectable BPC-157 on knee pain suggests the peptide could help repair tissue and regrow cartilage. However, the study followed just 16 participants, lacked a control group, and did not assess impacts on function or quality of life. An even smaller 2025 intravenous safety pilot on BPC-157 use involved 2 participants. While no adverse effects were reported during the short study, the researchers acknowledged that larger studies are needed to confirm safety. What is BPC-157\u00e2\u0080\u0099s regulatory status?The July 23\u00e2\u0080\u009324 FDA advisory vote added BPC-157 to the Section 503A bulk drug substances list, allowing pharmacies to include it in compounded medications.The FDA\u00e2\u0080\u0099s 8-6 vote, with one abstention, greenlit BPC-157 in both free-base and acetate forms.The recommendation did not make BPC-157 an FDA-approved drug, nor is it a component of an approved product. The federal health agency has yet to make final regulatory decisions on peptides.\u00e2\u0080\u009cRFK Jr. policies are hurting Americans,\u00e2\u0080\u009d Mandelbaum said. \u00e2\u0080\u009cThis decision is ridiculous. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s another step in the wrong direction. There\u00e2\u0080\u0099s no basis for any of this stuff.\u00e2\u0080\u009dIs the \u00e2\u0080\u0098Wolverine\u00e2\u0080\u0099 peptide safe?The safety profile of the Wolverine peptide for use in humans is largely unknown.As such, BPC-157 is banned by the World Anti-Doping Agency as an unapproved substance for athletes both in and out of competition. The FDA notes that peptides like BPC-157 (free base) may be sensitive to product formulation, processing, environmental conditions, and impurities, which could degrade the products and reduce their effectiveness.The health agency adds that it currently has limited safety information for how peptides like BPC-157 are administered. Soundararajan explained that his study was unable to estimate the incidence or overall safety of BPC-157 because adverse events were captured retrospectively from routine clinical notes and are likely underreported. \u00e2\u0080\u009cThat said, the medical records examined contain both positive and negative patient experiences,\u00e2\u0080\u009d he said. \u00e2\u0080\u009cMood, sleep, skin, injection-site, and gastrointestinal symptoms are concrete safety outcomes among the few examined patient records with available evidence that deserve prospective measurement and discussions by healthcare providers with their patients who report using BPC-157.\u00e2\u0080\u009dSome experts warn of short-term risks like infection at the injection site, but the long-term effects are not known.\u00e2\u0080\u009cWe don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t have publications of infections yet, but there are anecdotes of this,\u00e2\u0080\u009d Mandelbaum said. \u00e2\u0080\u009cPeople are injecting their joints with this stuff, and you have no idea what it is. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not standardized. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not being regulated by the FDA, and I think people should recognize that. And although we haven\u00e2\u0080\u0099t proven it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a safety hazard, we know it has no efficacy. So why do it? Why waste your money?\u00e2\u0080\u009dWhat to know before using unapproved peptidesExperts urge anyone considering BPC-157 or another peptide treatment to discuss it with their doctor first.You might ask for evidence supporting its use, information on its quality, and whether there are alternatives with established safety and effectiveness profiles.Mandelbaum noted there are many scientifically proven and safe alternatives to consider.\u00e2\u0080\u009cWe have spent the last 20 years developing an arsenal of biologics from PRP to bone marrow aspirate to adipose tissue to understanding glucosamine and hyaluronic acid,\u00e2\u0080\u009d he said. \u00e2\u0080\u009cWe\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve done an amazing job at studying these things. We\u00e2\u0080\u0099re getting to the point where we are understanding the complexities of biologics. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s exciting, and it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s impactful.\u00e2\u0080\u009d Mandelbaum vehemently opposed the use of unapproved peptides like BPC-157. He likened its rise in popularity to a \u00e2\u0080\u009cPonzi scheme\u00e2\u0080\u009d promoted by \u00e2\u0080\u009cgym rats\u00e2\u0080\u009d and \u00e2\u0080\u009cinternet influencers\u00e2\u0080\u009d who \u00e2\u0080\u009cleverage and exploit the gap between hope and knowledge.\u00e2\u0080\u009d Just because the FDA eased restrictions, he said, doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t make them any safer or more legitimate.That said, any use of unapproved peptides should also be disclosed to a doctor. \u00e2\u0080\u009cA short, open and empathetic clinical conversation can turn invisible consumer use of products like BPC-157 into useful clinical information that can critically help inform current and future care for such patients that ensure the best possible outcomes,\u00e2\u0080\u009d Soundararajan said.BPC-157 should not be combined with other experimental peptides until research determines the potential for adverse reactions or events. Long-term use of BPC-157 and other peptides marketed for wellness is not advised.", "content_hash": "df822ca46270e2c3e5b168d765a7ea4485b024ff5ae513ad9abc5a1c4ace344f", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:46.290972+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1411", "title": "Article II", "url": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/constitution/articleii", "final_url": "https://www.law.cornell.edu/constitution/articleii", "text": "Section 1.The executive power shall be vested in a President of the United States of America. He shall hold his office during the term of four years, and, together with the Vice President, chosen for the same term, be elected, as follows:Each state shall appoint, in such manner as the Legislature thereof may direct, a number of electors, equal to the whole number of Senators and Representatives to which the State may be entitled in the Congress: but no Senator or Representative, or person holding an office of trust or profit under the United States, shall be appointed an elector.The electors shall meet in their respective states, and vote by ballot for two persons, of whom one at least shall not be an inhabitant of the same state with themselves. And they shall make a list of all the persons voted for, and of the number of votes for each; which list they shall sign and certify, and transmit sealed to the seat of the government of the United States, directed to the President of the Senate. The President of the Senate shall, in the presence of the Senate and House of Representatives, open all the certificates, and the votes shall then be counted. The person having the greatest number of votes shall be the President, if such number be a majority of the whole number of electors appointed; and if there be more than one who have such majority, and have an equal number of votes, then the House of Representatives shall immediately choose by ballot one of them for President; and if no person have a majority, then from the five highest on the list the said House shall in like manner choose the President. But in choosing the President, the votes shall be taken by States, the representation from each state having one vote; A quorum for this purpose shall consist of a member or members from two thirds of the states, and a majority of all the states shall be necessary to a choice. In every case, after the choice of the President, the person having the greatest number of votes of the electors shall be the Vice President. But if there should remain two or more who have equal votes, the Senate shall choose from them by ballot the Vice President.The Congress may determine the time of choosing the electors, and the day on which they shall give their votes; which day shall be the same throughout the United States.No person except a natural born citizen, or a citizen of the United States, at the time of the adoption of this Constitution, shall be eligible to the office of President; neither shall any person be eligible to that office who shall not have attained to the age of thirty five years, and been fourteen Years a resident within the United States.In case of the removal of the President from office, or of his death, resignation, or inability to discharge the powers and duties of the said office, the same shall devolve on the Vice President, and the Congress may by law provide for the case of removal, death, resignation or inability, both of the President and Vice President, declaring what officer shall then act as President, and such officer shall act accordingly, until the disability be removed, or a President shall be elected.The President shall, at stated times, receive for his services, a compensation, which shall neither be increased nor diminished during the period for which he shall have been elected, and he shall not receive within that period any other emolument from the United States, or any of them.Before he enter on the execution of his office, he shall take the following oath or affirmation:--\"I do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully execute the office of President of the United States, and will to the best of my ability, preserve, protect and defend the Constitution of the United States.\"Section 2.The President shall be commander in chief of the Army and Navy of the United States, and of the militia of the several states, when called into the actual service of the United States; he may require the opinion, in writing, of the principal officer in each of the executive departments, upon any subject relating to the duties of their respective offices, and he shall have power to grant reprieves and pardons for offenses against the United States, except in cases of impeachment.He shall have power, by and with the advice and consent of the Senate, to make treaties, provided two thirds of the Senators present concur; and he shall nominate, and by and with the advice and consent of the Senate, shall appoint ambassadors, other public ministers and consuls, judges of the Supreme Court, and all other officers of the United States, whose appointments are not herein otherwise provided for, and which shall be established by law: but the Congress may by law vest the appointment of such inferior officers, as they think proper, in the President alone, in the courts of law, or in the heads of departments.The President shall have power to fill up all vacancies that may happen during the recess of the Senate, by granting commissions which shall expire at the end of their next session.Section 3.He shall from time to time give to the Congress information of the state of the union, and recommend to their consideration such measures as he shall judge necessary and expedient; he may, on extraordinary occasions, convene both Houses, or either of them, and in case of disagreement between them, with respect to the time of adjournment, he may adjourn them to such time as he shall think proper; he shall receive ambassadors and other public ministers; he shall take care that the laws be faithfully executed, and shall commission all the officers of the United States.Section 4.The President, Vice President and all civil officers of the United States, shall be removed from office on impeachment for, and conviction of, treason, bribery, or other high crimes and misdemeanors. \u2039 Article I up Article III \u203a", "content_hash": "d5bbf6e179a497865ce2f1e8c134acf05d3f476a454784dbe1d57e2416d61c8e", "domain": "law.cornell.edu", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:46.401460+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1412", "title": "Youth Leadership: NDIC, NILE University host immersion challenge for business school students", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=youth-leadership-ndic-nile-university-host-immersion-challenge-for-business-school-students", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=youth-leadership-ndic-nile-university-host-immersion-challenge-for-business-school-students", "text": "Youth Leadership: NDIC, NILE University host immersion challenge for business school students The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), in collaboration with Nile Business School, Nile University of Nigeria, has hosted a four-day Executive Industry Immersion Challenge (EIIC) aimed at bridging the gap between academic learning and practical industry experience. N NDIC May 21, 2026 1 min read Abuja, May 21, 2026: The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), in collaboration with Nile Business School, Nile University of Nigeria, has hosted a four-day Executive Industry Immersion Challenge (EIIC) aimed at bridging the gap between academic learning and practical industry experience.The programme, held at the NDIC Head Office in Abuja, provided business school students with valuable exposure to policy formulation, institutional governance, and public sector management.Speaking at the opening ceremony, the Managing Director/Chief Executive of NDIC, Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, described the initiative as a strategic platform for strengthening collaboration between academia and industry. He emphasised the importance of equipping future leaders with practical knowledge, ethical values, and sound leadership principles.The NDIC Chief Executive further encouraged participants to embrace integrity, transparency, and good governance as essential foundations for effective leadership and national development.The collaboration underscores NDIC\u2019s commitment to talent development, knowledge sharing, and the promotion of a financially stable and resilient society through meaningful partnerships with academic institutions. All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "efbc74e62562a26d736f77083aba047c6ee87c404e88ab62882c06f48faced3c", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:47.027818+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1413", "title": "Are Filtered Showerheads Really Worth It? The Best We Tested", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/best-showerhead-filter", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/best-showerhead-filter", "text": "The Fast Facts Filtered showerheads remove chlorine and heavy metals from shower water, which can help protect your skin barrier and improve hair quality, though they don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t actually soften hard water. Most people can benefit from budget-friendly options, but if your city uses chloramine to treat water, you may need a specialized filter like Filterbaby, which is also the only filter we\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve found that targets microplastics. Our testing revealed the weAqua filter as an effective and affordable option. Share on PinterestA quick look at the filtered showerheads and shower filters we testedA shower filter under $30 that works: weAqua Heavy Duty No BS Shower Filter\u00c2 |\u00c2 Skip to reviewExpensive but filters microplastics and chloramine: Filterbaby Showerhead Filter Pro\u00c2 |\u00c2 Skip to reviewA budget option that's a full showerhead: Brondell Nebia VivaSpring Filtered Showerhead\u00c2 |\u00c2 Skip to reviewA splurge that anecdotally improved acne better: Jolie Filtered Showerhead\u00c2 |\u00c2 Skip to reviewFiltered showerheads have been getting a makeover. Brands like Jolie and Filterbaby have ditched the \u00e2\u0080\u009cstraight outta Home Depot\u00e2\u0080\u009d aesthetic associated with most bathroom appliances.Instead, they\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve positioned them more like elite beauty devices. But is what\u00e2\u0080\u0099s inside any more effective than budget-friendly shower filters that have less unboxing appeal?After researching showerhead filter types, testing cheap and pricey options, and understanding what each removes, we think most people could benefit from a cheap filtered showerhead without needing to splurge.If your budget allows, you may gain extra perks, efficiency, and peace of mind by upgrading to a more expensive shower filter, like the Jolie or Filterbaby, but each comes with its own caveats.Four shower filters. Two Healthliners. Lots o\u00e2\u0080\u0099 research. Here\u00e2\u0080\u0099s what we learned.Share on PinterestLeft: tester\u00e2\u0080\u0099s skin before testing shower filters; Middle and right: tester\u00e2\u0080\u0099s skin and hair after using the weAqua shower filter. Photos courtesy of Kati Shy.Don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t buy one until you test your waterWe bought this quick home test kit from Amazon for both testers to take a before-and-after read on their shower water.It measures pH, hardness, lead and other heavy metals, chlorine, sulfates, and alkalinity. Granted, these test strips are less accurate than the more expensive, professional lab tests, but they will at least give you a baseline to consider.One tester\u00e2\u0080\u0099s water started off strong and was in range on every parameter except alkalinity and sulfates.Share on PinterestOur first tester\u00e2\u0080\u0099s water testing results before and after reviewing the filtered showerheads. Photo courtesy of Kati Shy.Our second tester\u00e2\u0080\u0099s baseline water was slightly out of range on in a few categories before she tested the filters, but overall, not terrible. She experienced more dramatic results to her skin, and the improvement in alkalinity may have been a factor. When she retested her water after trying shower filters, some of the heavy metals and chlorine levels on the color chart appeared more muted than before, suggesting that while the levels weren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t terrible to begin with, the filters may have brought them down even further.Share on PinterestOur second tester\u00e2\u0080\u0099s results before and after using filtered showerheads. Photos courtesy of Coral Clark.They don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t actually soften water, but they have other benefitsTo truly soften water, your filter has to remove calcium and magnesium particles that have already dissolved into your water. The showerheads we tested (and most others on the market) do not remove the minerals that are the root cause of hard water. Only home water softeners, salt-based systems, and reverse osmosis systems can remedy this.But that doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t mean shower filters are a lost cause. They remove chlorine and heavy metals, which benefits your skin barrier and hair quality. While newer research on how chlorine affects skin is more limited, dermatologists and experts tend to agree that it has adverse effects and is associated with dermatitis. We also spoke to Debra Sullivan, Ph.D., MSN, R.N., CNE, COI, who has been a nurse practitioner and nurse educator for more than 20 years. She flagged that heavy metals, well, throw red flags. \u00e2\u0080\u009cThere is substantial evidence that exposure to heavy metals negatively impacts both skin barrier integrity and hair health,\u00e2\u0080\u009d she said. Does that mean your shower water should be your new nemesis? No. But according to Sullivan, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s worth monitoring. \u00e2\u0080\u009cIt underscores the importance of monitoring and regulating environmental and cosmetic exposures to protect skin barrier function and hair health.\u00e2\u0080\u009dCheck to see if your city uses chlorine or chloramineSome cities treat water with chloramine instead of chlorine, and very few filtered showerheads or filter attachments actually filter out chloramine. Filterbaby is the only one we tested (full review below) that covers chloramines. The Afina shower head does as well, and it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a little cheaper than Filterbaby. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a full showerhead unit compared to Filterbaby, which is an attachment that works with your existing showerhead. Filterbaby is the only filter to prove it can filter microplastics. It publishes the raw lab data on its website. However, the Filterbaby does not use a KD-55 filter. This type of filter is known to work effectively against high water temperatures. So, if you choose the Filterbaby, opt for warm showers instead of hot ones (which is also better for your skin in many ways), or the filter may not be as effective.Bottom line: If your city treats water with chloramine, and about half of them do, it could be worth splurging on the Filterbaby or Afina. The expensive filters were only slightly easier to installJolie and Filterbaby showerheads both come with a handy wrench, so you don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t need to own tools to install them. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s a small detail, but a detail nonetheless.All four showerhead filters came with helpful visual instructions, and both testers were able to install them relatively smoothly.Filterbaby comes with a helpful bonus option to book a live video call with an installation expert through their app, if you need it.The filtered showerheads we recommendA shower filter under $30 that worksweAqua Heavy Duty No BS Shower FilterweAqua Heavy Duty No BS Shower FilterFilter type: KDF-55, coconut shell carbon, calcium sulfiteWhat it removes: chlorine, heavy metalsFilter replacement cost: $19.95 every 6 months (a 4-pack is $44.99)SHOP NOW AT AMAZONHealthline's reviewIf you're looking for an affordable filter to try out, this is a good option. It will defend against chlorine and heavy metals. This filter claims to remove 99.9% of them. Instead of a full showerhead, it's a filter attachment that works with your existing showerhead. But as you can see, it's not the most beautiful aesthetic.Our tester, who, according to a quick at-home test strip, turned out to have decent water to begin with, felt the filter made her hair feel noticeably softer and skin clearer. The results weren't dramatic, partly because her water was already in good shape, but helpful enough to justify a less-than-$30 purchase. It uses all three filter types that the more expensive Jolie showerhead includes.It claims to reduce fluoride as well, but our research suggests this may be unlikely and hard for any filter to do. The brand does perform third-party lab tests on its filters, but these results aren't publicly shared, so we can't wholly back the claim. Expensive but filters microplastics and chloramineFilterbaby Showerhead Filter ProFilterbaby Showerhead Filter ProFilter type: Ultrafiltration membrane, activated carbon fiberWhat it removes: chlorine, chloramines, heavy metals, VOCsFilter replacement cost: $42 every 2 to 3 monthsSHOP NOW AT FILTERBABYHealthline's reviewThis is the only filter we've found that uses a filter type capable of defending against chloramine in addition to chlorine. This is only beneficial if your city uses chloramine to treat water, so do a little homework before you decide to splurge. If you're spooked by forever chemicals like a lot of us these days, this filtered showerhead may appeal to you, because it can also filter microplastics. It is the most comprehensive filter on our list, but there is a catch. Because it doesn't use a KD-55 filter, it won't be as effective with hot water.Our tester's water, again, turned out to be less than alarming, so she didn't experience major skin-changing results. We recommend testing your water before you buy anything, but the peace of mind when it comes to microplastics may be enough of a reason to earn your purchasing power. A budget option that's a full showerheadBrondell Nebia VivaSpring Filtered ShowerheadBrondell Nebia VivaSpring Filtered ShowerheadFilter type: KDF-55What it removes: chlorine, heavy metalsFilter replacement cost: $16.99 every 6 monthsSHOP NOW AT AMAZONHealthline's reviewAnother budget-friendly option, it's worth noting because our tester was really in love with it before she switched to the more expensive Jolie filter, which ultimately won her over because it was more effective for her acne. That said, if you want an aesthetically pleasing showerhead filter, instead of just the filter attachment like the weAqua, and you want to keep it affordable, this one checks those boxes in addition to being effective. Our tester's skin felt silkier, and her hair was less frizzy. A splurge that anecdotally improved acne betterJolie Filtered ShowerheadJolie Filtered ShowerheadFilter type: KDF-55, coconut shell carbon, calcium sulfiteWhat it removes: chlorine, heavy metalsFilter replacement cost: $35 every 3 monthsSHOP NOW AT AMAZONHealthline's reviewAnother splurge option, but one that significantly improved our tester's acne compared to the Brondell above. They both filter the same elements, but Jolie uses additional filter types that could make it a more efficient and thorough filter head, stripping out more of the chlorine and heavy metals that can affect the skin barrier. If you're still not quite ready to splurge, our under $30 pick, the weAqua shower filter attachment, uses the same additional filter types. It could be worth trying before you decide to invest in the sleeker-looking Jolie.Share on PinterestLeft: tester\u00e2\u0080\u0099s skin after she stopped using the Jolie showerhead because she forgot to replace the filter. Right: her skin while using the filter. Photos courtesy of Coral Clark.Comparing filtered showerheads and what they actually filter outPriceOngoing filter costFilter type(s)ChlorineChloraminesHeavy metalsVolatile organic compounds (VOCs)WeAqua No BS Water Filter$25.95$19.95 every 6 months (less if you purchase a 4-pack)KDF-55, coconut shell carbon, calcium sulfiteyesnoyesnoBrondell Nebia VivaSpring$39.99$16.99 every 6 monthsKDF-55yesnoyesnoFilterbaby$159.99$42 every 2 to 3 monthsUltrafiltration Membrane, activated carbon fiberyesyesyesyesJolie$169.00$35 every 3 monthsKDF-55, coconut shell carbon, calcium sulfiteyesnoyesnoTo close this outWe\u00e2\u0080\u0099ve found that shower filters and filtered showerheads can improve skin and hair with varying results.But it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s worth noting that filtered showerheads may not filter out 100% of chlorine and heavy metals.Some of them (like weAqua) market that third-party laboratory testing has verified its 99.9% removal rate, but the brand does not publish results. In that way, buying a filtered showerhead requires a bit of blind faith (except for Filterbaby, which publishes the raw test results on its website).", "content_hash": "8a4cd0392f8f9023f08c0f4aea738b5df202ead562b6804cb41094a756fb89ac", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:49.268161+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1414", "title": "NDIC and Nile University, Immersion Challenge, Business School Students", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=ndic-nile-university-host-immersion-challenge-for-business-school-students", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=ndic-nile-university-host-immersion-challenge-for-business-school-students", "text": "NDIC and Nile University, Immersion Challenge, Business School Students N NDIC May 21, 2026 2 min read YOUTH LEADERSHIP: NDIC, NILE UNIVERSITY HOST IMMERSION CHALLENGE FOR BUSINESS SCHOOL STUDENTSThe Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) has reaffirmed its commitment to talent development and stronger industry-academia collaboration, through the platform of the Executive Industry Immersion Challenge (EIIC) programme that was conducted in partnership with the Nile Business School, Nile University of Nigeria, Abuja.Speaking at the opening ceremony of the 4-day programme at the Corporation\u2019s Head Office in Abuja, the Managing Director/Chief Executive of the NDIC, Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, described the initiative as strategic in addressing the widening gap between the academia and the business community.According to the NDIC Chief Executive, the rapidly evolving global work environment requires professionals who possess both theoretical knowledge and practical insight into the realities of the corporate world. In his words, \u201cthe Executive Industry Immersion Challenge has provided the NDIC with the opportunity of a practical platform to expose participants to real-world experience in policy formulation, institutional governance, and public sector management.\u201dThe Managing Director reiterated the commitment of the NDIC as a critical financial safety-net institution, to the promotion of financial system stability and enhancement of depositor confidence in the financial system. He urged participants, who are students of the executive NBA programme of the University, to embrace the positive values that will be learnt during the programme and adopt them as guiding principles for leadership and national development. He stressed that institutions can only command public confidence when their actions consistently reflect honesty, sound ethical conduct, good governance and transparency.The Project Coordinator of the programme for the NDIC and Director, Research, Policy & International Relations Department, Mr. Ibrahim Aliyu, explained that the EIIC had been consciously designed as an experiential learning initiative aimed at bridging the gap between theory and industry practice.In his remarks, the Dean of the Nile Business School, Prof. Hauwa Lamido, represented by a senior faculty member, Dr. Festus Ekechi stated that, the choice of the Corporation for the Industry Immersion Programme was informed by its footprint of sound corporate governance, professionalism and integrity in the nation\u2019s financial landscape. He assured that the School would take conscious steps toward integrating all the learning points from the exercise into its curriculum with a view to ensuring practical application the knowledge by the participants in their places of work. Hawwau GamboHead, Communication & Public Affairs Department All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "f63d0499c97d605c812c4b5e9e01b55027dce7acb8247ffaa408aaa8f53779af", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:49.791740+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1415", "title": "How to Manage Anxiety Before Your First Therapy Session", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/first-therapy-session", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/first-therapy-session", "text": "It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s natural to feel anxious before your first therapy session. Steps like considering what you want to discuss, preparing for the practical side of the appointment, and relaxation strategies may help reduce anxiety.Therapy is a common treatment option for various conditions, including mental health issues like depression and anxiety. No matter what type of therapy you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re having, it can bring up some tough conversations and feelings.It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not problematic to feel anxious before your first therapy session, but it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s worth knowing that there are things you can do that may help you feel more prepared and relaxed before the session starts.Is it normal to feel anxious before your first therapy session?It is completely natural to feel anxious or nervous before starting therapy.A 2022 study found that people typically experience challenging emotions when starting therapy, including fear and shame.For some people, these feelings may persist through several therapy sessions. You might feel worried about:displaying too much or too little emotionacting inappropriately during sessionsnot being a \u00e2\u0080\u009cgood\u00e2\u0080\u009d clienttalking about relevant experiencesworking through personal issues without being disloyal to loved onesYou might also feel anxious before a first therapy session because you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re unsure what to expect from the process.Some of these concerns may resolve when you start therapy and begin to build a trusting relationship with your therapist. Others, you may be able to prepare for in advance. The benefits of a consultation sessionKnowing what to expect during your first therapy session may help you feel less anxious when you attend.The exact contents of a first session may vary from person to person, depending on factors like:your therapistthe type of therapy, such as talk therapy or cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT)the location of therapy \u00e2\u0080\u0094 in-person or onlinewhy you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re attending therapyBefore officially starting therapy, you may need to attend one or more consultation sessions. These can allow you to learn the best type of therapy for you and determine whether a specific therapist is right for you.These consultation sessions may also be a good opportunity to find out from your therapist what a first session with them may involve. If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re feeling nervous about starting therapy, you can ask outright what to expect.Medical Perspective\u00e2\u0080\u009cConsultation sessions are opportunities for a potential client to ask questions of the potential therapist in order to gather enough information to decide whether or not to proceed in working with that particular individual. Both the client and therapist have a brief encounter to determine if they might be a good fit to work together. This contrasts with the typical nature of a first therapy session, in which the focus will be more on the therapist gathering diagnostic information about the client in order to begin creating a treatment plan.\u00e2\u0080\u009d\u00e2\u0080\u0094 Bethany Juby, PsyDLearn more: How to Find the Right Therapist for YouQuotes represent the opinions of our medical experts. All content is strictly informational and should not be considered medical advice.Tips to minimize anxiety before your first therapy sessionThe tips below may help you manage feelings of anxiety before your first official therapy session.Prepare for the practicalities of your appointmentBefore your first therapy session, it may relieve your anxiety to prepare for the practical elements of the appointment. This may include things like:driving the route to your therapist\u00e2\u0080\u0099s office or double-checking you have any video links for online therapychecking your insurance coverage for therapy, including details like your copay and deductiblesunderstanding how you will pay for the sessionfilling out any paperwork that your therapist requires you to bring to the sessionobtaining your health records from other healthcare professionals, if they are relevantwriting a list of questions you want to ask or topics you\u00e2\u0080\u0099d like to coverIn some cases, your therapist may ask you to arrive slightly early for your first session to fill out paperwork. Consider what you want to discussYour first therapy session is likely to involve your therapist getting to know you and understanding your goals in taking therapy. In some cases, this may take several sessions to establish.Your therapist may ask open questions to better understand what you hope to get out of therapy. Open questions are those that require a detailed answer instead of a simple \u00e2\u0080\u009cyes\u00e2\u0080\u009d or \u00e2\u0080\u009cno\u00e2\u0080\u009d response.Considering your therapy goals before your first session may help you feel more prepared for this conversation.Tips for answering open questionsThe following tips may help you feel more confident and comfortable answering open questions during your first therapy session:Don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t rush: Take a moment to really consider what your therapist is asking, how the question makes you feel, and what your answer is.Be honest: It might feel like you should tell your therapist what you believe they want to hear, but it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to be honest about your feelings and goals.Abandon perfectionism: Don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t worry if your answer feels jumbled or rambling. There are no wrong answers in therapy.Ask to revisit questions: If you don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t feel comfortable talking about something in your first session, ask your therapist if you can revisit the question at a later date.Get to know your therapistConsultation therapy sessions and early therapy sessions are important to understand if your therapist is well suited for your needs.A trusting, respectful relationship between you and your therapist is vital for you to develop and achieve your therapy goals. Part of this may involve finding a culturally competent and sensitive therapist.If you don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t think you will have a productive relationship with your therapist, it may be beneficial to consider a different practitioner.\u00c2\u00bbMore on this:The best therapy options for every budgetBe honest about your feelingsIf you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re feeling anxious before your first therapy session, it may be helpful to take some time to acknowledge your emotions. For some people, even naming the negative emotions you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re feeling can help relieve them. These feelings may or may not be something you feel happy talking about in your first therapy session.Try some stress-relieving practicesThe following practices may help reduce feelings of stress or anxiety:exercisesocialize with friends or loved onespractice some self-care, such as a warm bath or time on a hobby you enjoypractice gratitudeIt may also be helpful to avoid substances such as alcohol and caffeine.The bottom lineIt\u00e2\u0080\u0099s natural to feel anxious before your first therapy session, but that doesn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t mean there aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t ways you can manage and reduce that feeling.Consultation sessions are a good opportunity to understand if your therapist is suitable for your needs and to ask exactly what you can expect from the first few therapy sessions.Beyond this, it may also be helpful to prepare for the practicalities of therapy, consider what you want to discuss with your therapist, and try relaxation strategies.", "content_hash": "2a5d43b51a67dae271fc79504121fa25a5e80e1acb83121fe5df667ab53b0f1c", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:51.898118+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1416", "title": "NDIC, CDIC Taiwan Benchmark Deposit Insurance Experience", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-cdic-taiwan-benchmark-deposit-insurance-experience", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-cdic-taiwan-benchmark-deposit-insurance-experience", "text": "NDIC, CDIC Taiwan Benchmark Deposit Insurance Experience An NDIC delegation led by the Executive Director (Corporate Services), Mrs. Emily Osuji recently completed a study visit program with the Central Deposit Insurance Corporation (CDIC), Taiwan. N NDIC May 11, 2026 1 min read An NDIC delegation led by the Executive Director (Corporate Services), Mrs. Emily Osuji recently completed a study visit program with the Central Deposit Insurance Corporation (CDIC), Taiwan.The collaborative visit enabled the two organisations to benchmark each other in critical and emerging areas of the Deposit Insurance System (DIS) such as design, bank resolution frameworks, application of digital technologies and Artificial Intelligence as well as risk monitoring and early warning signals in DIS operations in particular and financial safety net in general.NDIC also exchanged views with Taiwan\u2019s SME Credit Guarantee Fund on strategies and framework to promote stability in the micro, small and medium enterprises sector of the economy.The visit provided a valuable platform to share Nigeria\u2019s experience and learn from global best practices.NDIC remains committed to leveraging international partnerships to strengthen depositor protection and enhance the resilience of Nigeria\u2019s financial system. All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "4545695af6c13c8b0d1551e5d8c270f4d61bdbb56bf031e82bed5fea534bf6e5", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:52.627222+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1417", "title": "Top 10 Benefits of Sleeping Naked", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/benefits-of-sleeping-naked", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/benefits-of-sleeping-naked", "text": "Key Takeaways Sleeping naked may help you fall asleep faster and improve sleep quality by lowering your body temperature, which is part of your body\u00e2\u0080\u0099s natural circadian rhythm. Better sleep from sleeping naked may support skin healing, reduce stress and anxiety, and lower your risk of weight gain, heart disease, and type 2 diabetes. Sleeping naked can promote vaginal health by reducing yeast infection risk and may increase male fertility by keeping testicles at an optimal temperature for sperm health. Sleeping naked might not be the first thing you think about when it comes to improving your health, but some benefits might be too good to ignore. Since sleeping naked is pretty easy to try yourself, it might be time to strip down and get your snooze on. For your health, that is. As it turns out, there are many benefits of sleeping naked. You may have heard of some of these, but others might surprise you.1. Fall asleep fasterYour body temperature is one key to how you fall asleep. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s actually part of your circadian rhythm, the biological rhythm that acts as your body\u00e2\u0080\u0099s \u00e2\u0080\u009cclock\u00e2\u0080\u009d for sleep. Cooling down tells your body that it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s time to sleep, so sleeping naked \u00e2\u0080\u0094 and allowing your body temperature to go down \u00e2\u0080\u0094 can actually help you fall asleep faster.2. Better sleep qualityNot only does cooling your body help you fall asleep faster, but it also improves your overall sleep quality. The ideal temperature for your bedroom is somewhere between 60\u00e2\u0080\u009367\u00c2\u00b0F (15 to 19\u00c2\u00b0C).One older 2012 study from the National Institutes of Health found that the temperature of the room where you sleep is one of the most important factors in achieving quality sleep.If it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s too cold or too hot, you risk impacting your rapid eye movement sleep, which is the dream stage of sleep that helps refresh your brain and body. Sleeping naked is one way to stay cool beneath the covers.3. Keeps skin healthyBecause sleeping naked can help increase your overall sleep quality, it can also improve your skin. One small 2018 study looked at whether poor sleep limited the skin\u00e2\u0080\u0099s ability to heal from a small wound.They split participants into three groups \u00e2\u0080\u0094 one that received \u00e2\u0080\u009cadequate\u00e2\u0080\u009d sleep, one that was sleep-deprived, and a third that was sleep-deprived but received extra nutrients. What they found was that the group that slept well recovered faster than the other two groups. And the extra nutrition? It didn\u00e2\u0080\u0099t make a significant difference in how fast the wounds healed.This shows that getting enough sleep could help your skin to recover and stay healthy, and if sleeping naked helps that happen, even better.4. Reduce stress and anxietyAnother reason sleeping naked might be a good change is that it could help reduce your overall stress and anxiety. It\u00e2\u0080\u0099s no secret that poor sleep has a major impact on your stress levels. A large 2020 study suggests that sleep disturbance can lead to persistent depressive symptoms and suicidal ideation in those who live with depression. While stress and anxiety can both cause insomnia, it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s important to remember that improving your sleep quality \u00e2\u0080\u0094 and getting enough sleep \u00e2\u0080\u0094 may help.5. Prevent weight gainNot sleeping well can have a range of health impacts.A 2022 review suggests that people who sleep seven or fewer hours per night are more likely to gain weight. Another way sleeping naked could help keep you trim? Keeping your body colder at night may help boost your calorie-burning abilities. A small study from 2014 following five men discovered that exposure to cooler temperatures, around 66\u00c2\u00b0F (19\u00c2\u00b0C), helped their bodies increase brown fat activity.6. Lower risk of heart disease and type 2 diabetesNot getting enough sleep can increase your risk of developing type 2 diabetes, according to a 2016 review. Having type 2 diabetes can, in turn, increase your risk of heart disease. By sleeping naked, you may increase your ability to fall asleep faster and stay asleep, which could make all the difference when it comes to your health.7. Promote vaginal healthSleeping naked is also a great way to increase vaginal health and avoid yeast infections. Tight-fitting or sweaty underwear can increase your risk of a vaginal yeast infection since yeast likes to grow in warm, moist places.Regardless of what you wear during the day, sleeping naked is an easy way to air out your vagina and keep it healthy.8. Increase male fertilityWomen aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t the only ones who can benefit from sleeping naked. A 2018 study of 656 males suggested a link between wearing tight-fitting underwear and lower sperm count. Men who reported wearing boxers had a higher sperm concentration and total sperm count than those who wore tight underwear.Sleeping naked is a great way to keep testicles cool and at an optimal temperature for sperm health.9. Boost self-esteemSleeping naked is also a great way to get in touch with your body and boost your self-esteem. A 2021 study suggests a link between time spent naked and increased body appreciation, which is definitely a win when it comes to embracing self-love.10. Improve your relationshipWhile sex can be a great part of your relationship, sleeping naked with your partner can be just as wonderful. In fact, one 2015 study discovered that skin-to-skin contact between adults stimulates the release of oxytocin, which plays an important role in building attachment between partners.Even better? Touching your partner is also great for your health \u00e2\u0080\u0094 not just your relationship \u00e2\u0080\u0094 and sleeping naked is a fantastic way to reap both benefits.The takeawayEven if you aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t comfortable sleeping completely naked, reducing the number of layers you wear at night \u00e2\u0080\u0094 or even just ditching your bra or underwear \u00e2\u0080\u0094 is an easy way to take advantage of these benefits.When it comes to sleep, the important thing is that you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re taking steps to ensure you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re getting enough good sleep.For more sleep support, check out our sleep shop.", "content_hash": "1fc76072fbcbd5c0b3ac27493bebd1e8611d08855b738df67aee7135e85afcb3", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:55.180900+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1418", "title": "Disposal of Landed Property, Microfinance Banks (In-Liquidation)", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=notice-to-general-public-for-disposal-of-landed-property-of-some-microfinance-bank-in-liquidation", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=notice-to-general-public-for-disposal-of-landed-property-of-some-microfinance-bank-in-liquidation", "text": "Disposal of Landed Property, Microfinance Banks (In-Liquidation) N NDIC April 16, 2026 3 min read 1.The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), in the exercise of its statutory mandate as the Liquidator of failed banks under section 62(1)(d) of NDIC Act, 2023 as amended, wishes to invite the general public for the upcoming disposal of Landed Properties belonging to some Micro Finance Banks (In-Liquidation) at 18 locations the Southern part of the country.Scope of Auction Exercise:2. The disposal process of the landed properties belonging to the Micro Finance Banks (In-Liquidation) shall be in a transparent and competitive bid. Bidders who wish to participate shall follow laid down guidelines which is aimed at ensuring, fair competition, accountability, equity and timeliness in line with tenets of corporate governance principles to enable value for money with commensurate financial returns from the auction exercise for the payment of liquidation dividends to uninsured depositors and creditors accordingly.3. Landed Property in the affected locations as listed below are to be be sold \u201cas is\u2019\u2019 and \u201cnet of all taxes\u2019\u2019.NDIC MICROFINANCE BANK PROPERTIESAKWA IBOMPrudential Co-Operative Microfinance Bank LimitedKm 5 Uyo-Ikot Ekpene Road, Essien Udom L.G.A \u2014 BungalowItam Market, Uyo \u2014 Lock Up ShopANAMBRAAguleri Microfinance Bank LimitedChief Idigo Road, Aguleri \u2014 1 Story BuildingUli Microfinance Bank LimitedOff Onitsha Owerri Express Way, Chukwumeka Odumegu Ojukwu University (University Junction) \u2014 BungalowOpposite Uli Micro Finance Bank, by Army Check Point \u2014 Undeveloped Parcel of land (approximately 4,500m\u00b2)CROSS RIVEROgoja Microfinance Bank Limited27 Mission Road, Igoli-Ogoja \u2014 BungalowIshibori Market, Ishibori, Ogoja \u2014 Undeveloped plot of land (697.152m\u00b2)New Agiga Layout, Barracks Road, No. 41, Mission Road, Igoli, Ogoja \u2014 6 Lock-up Shops on land (approximately 4,806.916m\u00b2)DELTAIC-Global Microfinance Bank Limited91, NDC Road, Opposite Aggs Ozoro, Isoko North LGA \u2014 3 Story Building40, Onasa Umusade, Opposite Ketstone Bank, Kwale, Ndokwa West LGA \u2014 Bungalow1, Ibrahim Kafas Road, Oleh, Isoko South LGA \u2014 1 Story BuildingIyede Microfinance Bank Limited1, Palace Road, Ekreme Quarters, Otor Iyede, Isoko North LGA \u2014 1 Story BuildingIMOMerit Microfinance Bank Limited21, Orlu Road, Amaigbo \u2014 1 Story BuildingOYOIfesowapo Microfinance Bank LimitedOkere Street, Oje Owode \u2014 BungalowIgangan Microfinance Bank LimitedNo. 1, Community Bank Road, Isale Akao, Igangan, Ibarapa LGA \u2014 BungalowReality Microfinance Bank LimitedReality House, Oladele George Street By Ap Filling Station, Sawmill, Old Ife Road, Ibadan \u2014 BungalowRIVERSSurelife Microfinance Bank LimitedBara-Oote in Deeyor Town, in Khana Local Government Area \u2014 Undeveloped plot of land (697.152m\u00b2)42, School Road, Azuabie Okujagu\u2013Ama, Port Harcourt \u2014 Undeveloped plot of land4. The auction exercise shall be open and competitive to all bidders and shall take place at NDIC Lagos Office, Asset Management Department, (9th Floor), Mamman Kontagora House, 23A, Marina, Lagos.5. All interested bidders should submit their sealed bids with 10% bid security in Bank Draft in favour of the closed Micro Finance Bank and drop at the NDIC Lagos Office, Asset Management Department, (9th Floor), Mamman Kontagora House, 23A, Marina, Lagos on or before 30th April, 2026. Failure to attach the 10% Bank Draft for bid security will render such bids submitted Null and Void.6. Successful bidder would be give two weeks from the date of the bid opening to pay the balance of 90% of the bided amount. Please note that any successful bid that failed to make final payment within the stipulated time frame shall forfeit their 10% amount as penalty charges.7. where they are sitting tenant or the property is on a long lease, the tenant OR lease holder would be given the right of first refusal- but subject to competitive bid.8. Submitted bids will be opened in the presence of all bidders on Thursday 30th April, 2026 by 12 noon prompt at the meeting Room, NDIC Lagos Office, (9th Floor), Mamman Kontagora House, 23A, Marina, Lagos.For further enquiries, please contact:Director, Asset Management Department,Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation, Lagos Office Annexe,(9th Floor), Mamman Kontagora House,23A, Marina,Lagos.Tel No: 08035925533. All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "7ac9b64908a2ce064f3f062140818410a421a86b99b5f0b46acf45390a7fee15", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:55.666290+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1419", "title": "How to Get a Prescription Refilled Without a Primary Care Doctor", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/how-to-get-prescription-refill-without-doctor", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/how-to-get-prescription-refill-without-doctor", "text": "Key takeaways If you have refills remaining on your prescription bottle, you can often request a refill directly from your pharmacy without talking with a doctor. Telehealth services like Teladoc, MDLIVE, or Amwell can connect you with licensed doctors who may refill your prescription after an online consultation. Controlled substances like opioids, attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) medications, and benzodiazepines typically require a new prescription from a healthcare professional, even if you take them regularly. You have a few options if you need a prescription refill but don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t have a primary care doctor.For example, you can visit an urgent care clinic, where a healthcare professional may review your medication and provide a refill. Telehealth services also offer online consultations with licensed doctors who can refill prescriptions if appropriate. They use electronic health records that help streamline the refill process and ensure safe prescribing.Also, many pharmacies offer limited prescription refills through their pharmacists for certain medications.Be sure to bring your prescription details and any relevant medical history to ensure a smooth process. However, controlled substances typically require a doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescription, and pharmacists can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t refill them.Check the prescription labelThe first step is to check the label on your prescription bottle. The label can show whether you have refills remaining, showing the number of refills (e.g., \u00e2\u0080\u009cRefills: 3\u00e2\u0080\u009d) and how long they\u00e2\u0080\u0099re valid. If you have refills left, you typically don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t need to consult a doctor for a new prescription \u00e2\u0080\u0094 you can simply contact your pharmacy to request a refill.However, certain medications, particularly controlled substances like opioids, medications for attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) (e.g., Adderall or Vyvanse), and benzodiazepines, often require a doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s visit for a new prescription. The Food and Drug Administration (FDA) highly regulates these medications, and you usually can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t get refills without a new prescription from a healthcare professional, even if you take them regularly.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:How to Refill a PrescriptionContact your pharmacy or prescribing physicianContact your pharmacy if you have refills left or need to check refill eligibility. Pharmacists play an important role in managing refill requests and can often address your needs efficiently, sometimes without needing approval from the doctor. A 2023 study showed that pharmacist-managed refill services can improve care while reducing the administrative burden on primary care physicians.If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re out of refills or need a new prescription, contact your prescribing physician to authorize more medication. For an emergency or one-time refill, some states and pharmacies allow you to be eligible under certain conditions:Emergency refills: If you run out of your medication and it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s critical to your health (e.g., heart medication or insulin), some pharmacies can issue a short-term refill without a doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s approval. This refill type usually requires proof that the medication is urgent.One-time refills: Some states have laws allowing pharmacies to provide a one-time refill for certain maintenance medications (like blood pressure or diabetes medication) without a new prescription, but only in certain situations, such as if you can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t reach your doctor immediately.To check your state\u00e2\u0080\u0099s laws on prescription refills and emergency refills:Check your state\u00e2\u0080\u0099s health department websiteVisit your state\u00e2\u0080\u0099s official health department website. They often provide information on prescription laws and regulations.Contact your pharmacyLocal pharmacists are well versed in the state\u00e2\u0080\u0099s prescription laws and can explain what\u00e2\u0080\u0099s allowed in your area.Call the prescribing doctor\u00e2\u0080\u0099s officeA healthcare professional can also advise you about relevant state laws or guide you to helpful resources.\u00c2\u00bbLearn more:8 Health Services Available at Your Local PharmacyMake an appointment with an online doctorYou may need to make an appointment with an online doctor for a medication refill in the following situations:No refills left: If your prescription has no refills remaining, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need a new prescription from a doctor.Medication changes: If you have side effects or if your condition changes, you may need to adjust your medication.Follow-up care: If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re due for a follow-up appointment to monitor your health condition or medication effectiveness, you may need a medication adjustment after the follow-up appointment.Lack of access to a primary care physician: If you don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t have a primary care doctor or can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t schedule an in-person appointment promptly, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need to have an online appointment with a doctor.Emergency situations: If you run out of critical medication and need an urgent refill but can\u00e2\u0080\u0099t reach your doctor, you\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll need a telehealth appointment so that a doctor can prescribe your refill.Convenience: If you prefer the convenience of telemedicine over an in-person visit, especially for routine refills or consultations, telemedicine may be a more effective way for you to get your refill.To make an appointment with an online doctor for a medication refill, follow these steps:Research telemedicine platforms: Look for reputable telemedicine services that have clear credentials and contact details. Many pharmacies also offer telehealth options.Sign up or log in: Create an account on the chosen platform or log in if you already have one. You may need to provide personal information, including your medical history and current medications.Schedule an appointment: Select a time that works for you. Some platforms offer same-day appointments, while others may require a few days\u00e2\u0080\u0099 notice.Prepare for the consultation: During the appointment, be ready to discuss your current medications, any side effects you may be experiencing, and your overall health.Follow up if needed: After your consultation, the doctor can send a prescription directly to your pharmacy. Ask your doctor or pharmacist questions to ensure you understand the instructions they provide regarding your medication.\u00c2\u00bbOnline Care:Get prescribed medication refills for a range of conditions in as little as 15 minutes with Optum Perks.Optum Perks is owned by RVO Health. By clicking on this link, we may receive a commission. Learn more.What\u00e2\u0080\u0099s next?If you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re running out of your medication and don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t think you can access a doctor in person, here are some places to start to get a refill:Check your prescription label for refill details and validity.Contact your pharmacy first to confirm refill availability and eligibility.Explore telehealth services for quick online consultations and refills.Visit an urgent care clinic if you need an in-person evaluation for a refill.Research state-specific laws on emergency or one-time refills for your medication.Prepare your medical history and prescription details before requesting a refill.Consider switching to a pharmacy with robust refill services if you frequently need refills.Don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t wait until you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re out of your meds before looking into a refill.Disclaimer: While Healthline strives for factual, comprehensive, and current consumer drug information, this article is not a substitute for a licensed healthcare professional\u00e2\u0080\u0099s expertise. Always consult a doctor before taking or discontinuing any medication. Drug information is subject to change and may not cover all uses, directions, precautions, warnings, interactions, reactions, or adverse effects. The lack of a warning does not guarantee a drug\u00e2\u0080\u0099s safety, effectiveness, or appropriateness for all patients or specific uses. Learn more about our approach to content integrity.", "content_hash": "4cef526715e3d59a4d62e99faf232ecc9702d8be862d03ba505470e3a9aa21bc", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:58.193717+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1420", "title": "Resolution of Failed Banks: NDIC Commences Process to Conclude the Liquidation of 89 MFBs & PMB", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=resolution-of-failed-banks-ndic-commences-process-to-conclude-the-liquidation-of-89-mfbs-pmb", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=resolution-of-failed-banks-ndic-commences-process-to-conclude-the-liquidation-of-89-mfbs-pmb", "text": "Resolution of Failed Banks: NDIC Commences Process to Conclude the Liquidation of 89 MFBs & PMB N NDIC April 15, 2026 5 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) has commenced the process of concluding the liquidation activities of 89 closed Microfinance Banks (MFBs) and Primary Mortgage Banks (PMBs) following their successful acquisition by new owners under the Purchase and Assumption (P&A) resolution model executed by the Corporation.The 89 closed banks were part of the 179 MFBs and 4 PMBs whose banking licenses were revoked by the Central Bank of Nigeria (CBN) on May 22nd and 23rd, 2023. Through the Purchase and Assumption agreements, 89 new eligible institutions were issued licenses by the CBN, to acquire the assets and liabilities of the defunct banks and have since commenced operations under new names.In order to legally conclude the liquidation process in accordance with the provisions of its enabling Act and other relevant laws, the NDIC in its capacity as the Liquidator of the defunct banks, will be presenting applications to various Judicial divisions of the Federal High Court to obtain orders of dissolution for the closed banks and to release the Corporation as Liquidator.The list of the defunct banks and assuming new banks are as follows:NDIC MICROFINANCE BANK NAME CHANGES - DEFUNCT AND ASSUMING BANKSABIAMouau Vasmucs Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Movasco-OP Microfinance Bank LimitedAKWA IBOMEduek Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Mint Microfinance Bank LimitedIni Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Uforo Microfinance Bank LimitedNsehe Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Vista Microfinance Bank LimitedZawadi Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Zitra Microfinance Bank LimitedADAMAWAAdamawa Homes & Savings Ltd \u2192 Adamawa Mortgage Bank LtdMautech Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Modibbo Adama University Microfinance Bank LimitedMichika Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Premier Microfinance Bank LimitedBiyama Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Dabtikir Microfinance Bank LimitedANAMBRAAkpo Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Oganiru Microfinance Bank LimitedAnya Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Pionner (Diohaunoego) Microfinance Bank LimitedAwka Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Plantinum Microfinance Bank LimitedEnugwu-Ukwu Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Umunri Microfinance Bank LimitedIsi-Aku Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Isiego Microfinance Bank LimitedObosi Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Adike Microfinance Bank LimitedBENUEBipc Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Novus Microfinance Bank LimitedJamis Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Strait Sahara Microfinance Bank LimitedDELTACub Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Unicoop Microfinance Bank LimitedUmejei Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Kolisa Microfinance Bank LimitedEDOAbc Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Okada Microfinance Bank LimitedEhor Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ehinoma Microfinance Bank LimitedEsan Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ubj Microfinance Bank LimitedEKITIAmoye Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ikere Microfinance Bank LimitedENUGUGoldenfunds Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Royal Excellent Microfinance Bank LimitedFCTMainsail Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Duxbank Microfinance Bank LimitedAlly Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ultraviolet Microfinance Bank LimitedBusiness Support Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Transpay Microfinance Bank LimitedThe Daniels Global Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Swifttrust Microfinance Bank LimitedFirst Multiple Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Koboweb Microfinance Bank LimitedIMOEvangel Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Vangel Microfinance Bank LimitedGreenland Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 5TT Microfinance Bank LimitedJIGAWANew World Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 BKD New Microfinance Bank LimitedKADUNANarict Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Basawa Microfinance Bank LimitedFahimta Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Cedrus Microfinance Bank LimitedMabinas Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Al'Hikma Microfinance Bank LimitedKANOGrassroots Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 MIA Microfinance Bank LimitedNorthbridge Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Esteem Microfinance Bank LimitedKATSINACherish Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Cool Microfinance Bank LimitedKWARAOmu-Aran Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Olomu Aperan Microfinance Bank LimitedLAGOSArise Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Shine Microfinance Bank LimitedBanccorp Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Bloc Microfinance Bank LimitedBishopgate Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Advancly Microfinance Bank LimitedBridgeway Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Bway Microfinance Bank LimitedBriyth Covenant Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Weston\u2013Charis Microfinance Bank LimitedCredit Afrique Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Kaizen Microfinance Bank LimitedEcho Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Plus One Microfinance Bank LimitedEyowo Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Entrepreneur Microfinance Bank LimitedFiyinfolu Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Teerus Microfinance Bank LimitedHackman Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Lightway Microfinance Bank LimitedHalmond Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Casa Microfinance Bank LimitedManna Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Savesimple Microfinance Bank LimitedManny Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Silverend Microfinance Bank LimitedMayfair Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Optimun Global Microfinance Bank LimitedMercury Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Dash Microfinance Bank LimitedMoneywise Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Indulge Microfinance Bank LimitedNetwork Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Unicorn Microfinance Bank LimitedNuture Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 MBAG Microfinance Bank LimitedOnyx Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Digitvant Microfinance Bank LimitedOros Capital Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ezpay Microfinance Bank LimitedPeniel Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Zircon Microfinance Bank LimitedPrimera Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Koins Microfinance Bank LimitedPurple Money Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Willows Microfinance Bank LimitedStallion Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Springfield Microfinance Bank LimitedSunrise Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Stable Microfinance Bank LimitedSurbpolitan Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Charis Microfinance Bank LimitedVerdant-Capital Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Verdant Microfinance Bank LimitedZikado Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Avest Microfinance Bank LimitedNASARAWAJosad Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Payrep Microfinance Bank LimitedNIGERMusharaka Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Muamala Microfinance Bank LimitedDangizhi Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Metro Express Network Microfinance Bank LimitedEdumana Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Edusoko Microfinance Bank LimitedOGUNAiyepe Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Springville Microfinance Bank LimitedInterland Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Nexton Microfinance Bank LimitedStar Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Sosa Microfinance Bank LimitedZigate Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Katsu Microfinance Bank LimitedONDOFasilidapo Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ourpass Microfinance Bank LimitedNewage Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Cashbrite Microfinance Bank LimitedOSUNBoluwaduro Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Afole Microfinance Bank LimitedIba Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Bankeasy Microfinance Bank LimitedIdese Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Sofaj Microfinance Bank LimitedOla Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Run Microfinance Bank LimitedOlofin Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 DSC Microfinance Bank LimitedOlofin-Owena Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Avantus Microfinance Bank LimitedOsogbo Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Bold Microfinance Bank LimitedOYOFirstindex Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ricia Capital Microfinance Bank LimitedJoint Farmers Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Tellerone FI Microfinance Bank LimitedOlogbon Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Akata Microfinance Bank LimitedPLATEAUBluewhales Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ellington Microfinance Bank LimitedRIVERSIwoama Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Tenn Bank LimitedHawwau GamboHead, Communication & Public Affairs All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "0db59b58649a670ab7e88870771fee2acad7b4aec32a778a44db500e082b1806", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:58.764504+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1421", "title": "What Is Hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia?", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia", "text": "Key takeawaysHippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia refers to the phobia or fear of long words. Organizations may consider it a type of specific phobia or social anxiety disorder. People with hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia may experience feelings of shame or fear of ridicule for mispronouncing long words, which may cause distress or anxiety. They may avoid reading to prevent encountering long words.Anyone who experiences fear or anxiety when they encounter long words may benefit from working with a healthcare professional. Cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) and other treatment options may be helpful.Hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia is one of the longest words in the dictionary \u00e2\u0080\u0094 and, in an ironic twist, is the name for a fear of long words. Sesquipedalophobia is another term for the phobia. Healthcare organizations may consider hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia a type of specific or simple phobia, which is an irrational, intense fear of something that poses no or very little danger.Alternatively, they may consider it a type of social anxiety disorder, formerly called social phobia, which involves a fear or judgment from others.What are the symptoms of hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia?A person with hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia may experience symptoms when they see a long word, such as \u00e2\u0080\u009cantidisestablishmentarianism.\u00e2\u0080\u009d This can cause feelings of fear and anxiety. The person may also avoid reading so they don\u00e2\u0080\u0099t encounter long words that\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll cause them to panic.Anecdotal evidence suggests that the fear of long words can trigger embarrassment or feelings of being mocked when pronouncing or reading long words. Other symptoms may include:tremblingsweatingdizzinessfaintingdry mouthheadachetrouble breathingfeeling distressed over academics or work involving long wordsThere are also more general phobia symptoms that you could watch out for, including:being aware that the phobia is unreasonable, but feeling powerless to control your fearunable to function as you usually would because of your phobianauseaWhat can cause specific phobias?Not much is known about what causes this and other types of specific phobia. But there are some causes and risk factors that are common across multiple phobias.These include:An associated negative event: For example, a person who had a hard time learning words as a child may panic whenever they see a long word. Their difficulty learning words could be a scary, traumatic time.Genetics: People who have a family history of certain phobias, anxiety, of other mental health conditions may have a higher chance of developing the same kind of phobia.Environment: This phobia may also be triggered by learned behavior, such as hearing about negative experiences related to that specific phobia or traumatic experiences related to it.How do doctors diagnose hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia?Some individuals with specific phobias may never seek out medical help. Instead, they may persistently avoid situations related to the thing they are fearful of.For example, people with hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia may take jobs where they aren\u00e2\u0080\u0099t exposed to lengthy words and phrases.However, it can be helpful to speak with a healthcare professional, particularly if symptoms become unbearable or other symptoms emerge. Your doctor will ask you questions about your symptoms to determine if you have a phobia or anxiety disorder. They\u00e2\u0080\u0099ll also review your psychiatric, medical, family, and social history. The Diagnostic and Statistical Manual of Mental Disorders (DSM-5) outlines a very specific definition for social phobias. Medical professionals use the DSM-5 to help them make diagnoses.The table below outlines the DSM-5 criteria for specific phobias and social anxiety disorder:Specific phobiaSocial anxiety disorder\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 fear or anxiety about a specific object or situation \u00e2\u0080\u00a2 the object or situation almost always causes an immediate feeling of fear or anxiety\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 the person actively avoids the situation that causes them fear or anxiety\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 the fear or anxiety is disproportionate to the danger that the situation actually poses\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 feelings of fear or anxiety last for at least 6 months\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 fear, anxiety, or avoidance causes clinically significant distress or adversely affects social or occupational functioning\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 the person\u00e2\u0080\u0099s symptoms are not due to another condition \u00e2\u0080\u00a2 fear or anxiety of at least one social situation in which someone may be exposed to potential scrutiny from others\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 fear of acting in a way that others may perceive negatively\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 the social situation causes feelings of anxiety or fear \u00e2\u0080\u00a2 the person feel fear or anxiety during the situation or will avoid it entirely\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 fear and anxiety are disproportionate to the danger of the situation\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 avoidance, fear, or anxiety lasts at least 6 months and causes significant distress or affects regular functioning\u00e2\u0080\u00a2 fear is not due to another condition or substancefear or anxiety around 1 or multiple social situations where a person is possibly exposed to the possible scrutiny of othersWhat treatment options are available for hippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia?Cognitive behavioral therapy (CBT) is typically the first treatment option for phobias. CBT blends exposure therapy with other therapeutic techniques in order to help you cope with your anxiety. This version of psychotherapy helps change your response to the object, situation, or word causing you fear and anxiety.Medications may also be helpful in managing anxiety disorders. However, not much is known about their effectiveness in treating this particular phobia.Other treatment options include:talk therapy with a psychiatrist, counselor, or social workermindfulness strategies such as mindful breathing, listening, and observation to help you cope with anxietyattending a support group to connect with other people facing the same or similar phobia\u00c2\u00bbFIND CARE:Find a mental health professional in your area today.Management strategiesYou may be able to manage symptoms of anxiety by making certain lifestyle changes, such as:getting enough sleep each nighteating a healthy and balanced dietcutting out substances that can make anxiety worse, like caffeinefacing fearful and anxiety-inducing situations head-onWhen confronted with long words, you may also find it helpful to:Substitute words: Avoiding long words may help you cope, but it\u00e2\u0080\u0099s not necessarily possible all the time. If faced with a long word, try substituting it with a similar shorter term. For example, if you need to write \u00e2\u0080\u009crefrigerator,\u00e2\u0080\u009d use \u00e2\u0080\u009cfridge\u00e2\u0080\u009d instead. You could also try and replace a friend\u00e2\u0080\u0099s long name with their initials or nickname, as long as they\u00e2\u0080\u0099re OK with it.Break words down: Take your time when reading a long word. Breathe in and break the word down into parts, then into syllables. For example, if you have a word like \u00e2\u0080\u009csemiautobiographical,\u00e2\u0080\u009d read it as sem-i-au-to-bi-o-gra-phi-cal.Take advantage of technology: Computers, smartphones, and other electronic devices have autocorrect and dictionaries available to help with spelling. They may also help with phonetic pronunciation in the event that you must learn to pronounce a long word.Online therapy optionsRead our review of the best online therapy options to find the right fit for you.The bottom lineHippopotomonstrosesquippedaliophobia is a fear of long words. People may experience distress and anxiety when they encounter long words due to concerns about judgment from others.More research is necessary to better understand the fear of long words and what happens when a person is exposed to triggers.Speak with your doctor or a counselor if you\u00e2\u0080\u0099re experiencing symptoms. They can help you get to the bottom of your fear, understand your symptoms, and come up with a treatment plan. Friends, family, and therapy groups can also help you cope with your phobia.", "content_hash": "fd40c574b9aff0b09a072e2ec44957f6522f0a64675a2e6aeb09e97858104aef", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:01.261360+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1422", "title": "Notice of Intention to Terminate Liquidation Activities", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=notice-of-intention-to-terminate-liquidation-activities", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=notice-of-intention-to-terminate-liquidation-activities", "text": "Notice of Intention to Terminate Liquidation Activities N NDIC April 8, 2026 5 min read NOTICE is hereby given to the General Public by the Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) in its capacity as the Liquidator of the under listed closed Microfinance and Primary Mortgage Institutions, that the Corporation in accordance with the provisions of its enabling law and other relevant laws , will at the expiration of thirty (30) days from the date of this publication , be presenting applications to the various Judicial divisions of the Federal High Court to obtain orders of dissolution for these closed banks and to release/discharge the Corporation as Liquidator of these banks at the expiration of thirty (30) days from the date of this publication.SCHEDULE OF BANKS FOR DISSOLUTIONNDIC MICROFINANCE BANK NAME CHANGESABIAMouau Vasmucs Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Movasco-OP Microfinance Bank LimitedAKWA IBOMEduek Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Mint Microfinance Bank LimitedIni Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Uforo Microfinance Bank LimitedNsehe Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Vista Microfinance Bank LimitedZawadi Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Zitra Microfinance Bank LimitedANAMBRAAkpo Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Oganiru 