Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Springfield Microfinance Bank LimitedSunrise Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Stable Microfinance Bank LimitedSurbpolitan Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Charis Microfinance Bank LimitedVerdant-Capital Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Verdant Microfinance Bank LimitedZikado Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Avest Microfinance Bank LimitedNASARAWAJosad Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Payrep Microfinance Bank LimitedNIGERMusharaka Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Muamala Microfinance Bank LimitedDangizhi Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Metro Express Network Microfinance Bank LimitedEdumana Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Edusoko Microfinance Bank LimitedOGUNAiyepe Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Springville Microfinance Bank LimitedInterland Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Nexton Microfinance Bank LimitedStar Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Sosa Microfinance Bank LimitedZigate Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Katsu Microfinance Bank LimitedONDOFasilidapo Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ourpass Microfinance Bank LimitedNewage Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Cashbrite Microfinance Bank LimitedOSUNBoluwaduro Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Afole Microfinance Bank LimitedIba Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Bankeasy Microfinance Bank LimitedIdese Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Sofaj Microfinance Bank LimitedOla Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Run Microfinance Bank LimitedOlofin Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 DSC Microfinance Bank LimitedOlofin-Owena Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Avantus Microfinance Bank LimitedOsogbo Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Bold Microfinance Bank LimitedOYOFirstindex Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ricia Capital Microfinance Bank LimitedJoint Farmers Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Tellerone FI Microfinance Bank LimitedOlogbon Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Akata Microfinance Bank LimitedPLATEAUBluewhales Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Ellington Microfinance Bank LimitedRIVERSIwoama Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Tenn Bank LimitedADAMAWAAdamawa Homes & Savings Ltd \u2192 Adamawa Mortgage Bank LtdMautech Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Modibbo Adama University Microfinance Bank LimitedMichika Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Premier Microfinance Bank LimitedBiyama Microfinance Bank Limited \u2192 Dabtikir Microfinance Bank LimitedHawwau GamboHead, Communication & Public Affairs All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "8869a9d4e64b3df2e9a75156c01f992206247fdf67e31bf8b4970dc41bfdf82a", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:01.882467+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1423", "title": "Breathwork Meditation for Better Sleep During Perimenopause", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/calm-your-mind-breathwork-meditation-for-better-sleep-during-perimenopause", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/calm-your-mind-breathwork-meditation-for-better-sleep-during-perimenopause", "text": "Breathwork Meditation for Better Sleep During Perimenopause Skip to main contentSubscribeHealth ConditionsHealth ConditionsAlzheimer's DiseaseBreast CancerCancer CareChronic Kidney DiseaseChronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD)Colon CancerDigestive HealthEczemaEye HealthHeart HealthMenopauseMental HealthMigraineMultiple Sclerosis (MS)Parkinson's DiseasePsoriasisRheumatoid Arthritis (RA)Sleep HealthType 2 DiabetesWeight ManagementWellnessWellness TopicsAllergiesCBDFitnessMen's WellnessMental Well-BeingNutritionParenthoodSexual HealthSkin CareVitamins and SupplementsWomen's WellnessMedicationsPrescription MedicationsBotoxDupixentEyleaGLP-1sRepathaRexultiSkyriziTrintellixUbrelvyVraylarProduct ReviewsProduct ReviewsAt-Home TestingCBDFitnessMen's HealthMental HealthNutritionSleepVitamins and SupplementsWomen's HealthResourcesToolsA1C ExplorerCalorie CalculatorMacronutrient CalculatorPill IdentifierSleep CalculatorEngageBezzy CommunitiesDaily Dose LessonsGLP-1 GuideHealth NewsNewslettersRecipesVideo LibraryJoin our communityFollow Healthline on our socials for all things health.Find a DoctorFindCareCardiologyDentistryDermatologyNeurologyOB-GYNOrthopedic SurgeryPediatricsPrimary CarePsychiatryUrologySearch HealthlineSubscribeMenopauseThe BasicsTreatmentTreatmentMedications for MenopauseSymptom ManagementSymptom ManagementAutonomic & VasomotorBone & Musculoskeletal HealthGut HealthSexual HealthHeart HealthWeight ManagementWeight ManagementDiet & NutritionFitnessHolistic HealthMental Well-BeingNavigating IntimacyResources for Doctors' VisitsEarly Menopause Share this article\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.About UsContact UsTerms of UsePrivacy NoticePrivacy SettingsAdvertising PolicyLicensing RequestsHealth TopicsSitemapMedical AffairsContent IntegrityNewslettersYour Privacy Choices\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.AboutCareersAdvertise with usOUR BRANDSHealthlineMedical News TodayGreatistPsych CentralBezzy", "content_hash": "708fe1671196b8b86f2312f7c7aa0c40160eb576dd3ddc31a1d6c33399af5132", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:04.640785+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1424", "title": "NDIC Provides Educational Platform for Students on Financial System Stability", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-provides-educational-platform-for-students-on-financial-system-stability", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-provides-educational-platform-for-students-on-financial-system-stability", "text": "NDIC Provides Educational Platform for Students on Financial System Stability The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) hosted students from Ibrahim Badamasi Babangida University, Lapai, Niger State, on an educational visit to its Head Office. N NDIC April 7, 2026 1 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) hosted students from Ibrahim Badamasi Babangida University, Lapai, Niger State, on an educational visit to its Head Office. The visit provided students with practical insights into the Corporation's structure, operations, and critical role in Nigeria's financial system.During the comprehensive visit, students received detailed presentations on the NDIC's core mandates: deposit insurance, bank supervision, and distress resolution and bank liquidation. These presentations were designed to give students academic context and practical understanding of how the Corporation fulfills its statutory responsibilities.Participants engaged in interactive sessions that deepened their understanding of the NDIC's role in maintaining financial system stability. These discussions enabled students to connect theoretical knowledge from their academic programs with real-world applications in financial regulation and depositor protection.The educational initiative reflects the NDIC's commitment to building awareness among the younger generation about the importance of deposit insurance and financial system safety. By providing university students with direct exposure to the Corporation's operations, the NDIC contributes to developing a knowledgeable workforce for Nigeria's financial services sector.Such educational visits serve multiple purposes: they demystify the operations of financial regulatory bodies, create career awareness among students, and foster understanding of how institutions like the NDIC protect the interests of ordinary Nigerians. Students gain firsthand knowledge of the complex processes involved in bank supervision, resolution of failed institutions, and liquidation procedures.The NDIC's investment in student education demonstrates institutional commitment to developing human capital and promoting financial literacy across Nigeria's educational institutions. All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "d6ef351eb5f7cb8994805fa321f3829a3e3be861c0ca74d80161a8b6ba9ff954", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:05.233424+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1425", "title": "Mediterranean Diet for Beginners", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/mediterranean-diet-for-beginners", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/mediterranean-diet-for-beginners", "text": "Mediterranean Diet for Beginners Skip to main contentSubscribeHealth ConditionsHealth ConditionsAlzheimer's DiseaseBreast CancerCancer CareChronic Kidney DiseaseChronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD)Colon CancerDigestive HealthEczemaEye HealthHeart HealthMenopauseMental HealthMigraineMultiple Sclerosis (MS)Parkinson's DiseasePsoriasisRheumatoid Arthritis (RA)Sleep HealthType 2 DiabetesWeight ManagementWellnessWellness TopicsAllergiesCBDFitnessMen's WellnessMental Well-BeingNutritionParenthoodSexual HealthSkin CareVitamins and SupplementsWomen's WellnessMedicationsPrescription MedicationsBotoxDupixentEyleaGLP-1sRepathaRexultiSkyriziTrintellixUbrelvyVraylarProduct ReviewsProduct ReviewsAt-Home TestingCBDFitnessMen's HealthMental HealthNutritionSleepVitamins and SupplementsWomen's HealthResourcesToolsA1C ExplorerCalorie CalculatorMacronutrient CalculatorPill IdentifierSleep CalculatorEngageBezzy CommunitiesDaily Dose LessonsGLP-1 GuideHealth NewsNewslettersRecipesVideo LibraryJoin our communityFollow Healthline on our socials for all things health.Find a DoctorFindCareCardiologyDentistryDermatologyNeurologyOB-GYNOrthopedic SurgeryPediatricsPrimary CarePsychiatryUrologySearch HealthlineSubscribeNutritionMeal KitsOverviewDietsMeal KitsPrepared MealsComparisonsGrocery DeliverySpecial DietsHealthy EatingFood FreedomConditionsFeel Good FoodProductsVitamins & SupplementsSustainabilityWeight Management Share this article\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.About UsContact UsTerms of UsePrivacy NoticePrivacy SettingsAdvertising PolicyLicensing RequestsHealth TopicsSitemapMedical AffairsContent IntegrityNewslettersYour Privacy Choices\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.AboutCareersAdvertise with usOUR BRANDSHealthlineMedical News TodayGreatistPsych CentralBezzy", "content_hash": "8b08841777a458d0218bf4e466f36dc8dab8d7886cf2aadfd2e1bcb36d1e3f5f", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:07.766510+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1426", "title": "NDIC Hosts Deposit Protection Fund Uganda on Strategic Study Visit Program", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-hosts-deposit-protection-fund-uganda-on-strategic-study-visit-program", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-hosts-deposit-protection-fund-uganda-on-strategic-study-visit-program", "text": "NDIC Hosts Deposit Protection Fund Uganda on Strategic Study Visit Program The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) hosted the Board and Management of the Deposit Protection Fund (DPF) of Uganda on a comprehensive five-day study visit program. N NDIC April 2, 2026 1 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) hosted the Board and Management of the Deposit Protection Fund (DPF) of Uganda on a comprehensive five-day study visit program. The visit provided Ugandan counterparts with key insights into the critical activities and achievements of the NDIC as a strategic regional leader in deposit insurance.The study program was designed to showcase the NDIC's operational excellence in depositor protection and demonstrate best practices that have established the Corporation as a recognized leader within the African deposit insurance community. The five-day format allowed sufficient time for detailed discussions, facility tours, and comprehensive knowledge transfer across various functional areas.Through this engagement, the DPF Uganda gained practical understanding of the NDIC's strategies for maintaining high coverage of depositor accounts, managing bank resolution processes efficiently, and implementing risk monitoring frameworks. The visit also provided opportunities to discuss common challenges faced by African deposit insurers and explore collaborative solutions.Such bilateral visits strengthen regional cooperation within the African deposit insurance community and facilitate the exchange of best practices among institutions with similar mandates. By hosting international delegations, the NDIC positions itself as a knowledge center and institutional leader capable of sharing experiences with peer organizations.The strategic visit demonstrates the NDIC's commitment to regional cooperation and institutional capacity building across Africa's financial sector. These engagements contribute to strengthening deposit insurance systems continent-wide, ultimately benefiting millions of depositors across the region.The successful hosting of the DPF Uganda delegation reinforces the NDIC's reputation as a credible, professional institution dedicated to advancing deposit insurance excellence throughout Africa. All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "8fc1b7a1806fe792e0aa8a02f79ee4cb797f4cb44712120ebd6d0fd49be354e2", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:08.308870+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1427", "title": "Lower Back Stretches to Reduce Pain and Build Strength", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/lower-back-stretches-to-reduce-pain-and-build-strength", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/lower-back-stretches-to-reduce-pain-and-build-strength", "text": "Lower Back Stretches to Reduce Pain and Build Strength Skip to main contentSubscribeHealth ConditionsHealth ConditionsAlzheimer's DiseaseBreast CancerCancer CareChronic Kidney DiseaseChronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD)Colon CancerDigestive HealthEczemaEye HealthHeart HealthMenopauseMental HealthMigraineMultiple Sclerosis (MS)Parkinson's DiseasePsoriasisRheumatoid Arthritis (RA)Sleep HealthType 2 DiabetesWeight ManagementWellnessWellness TopicsAllergiesCBDFitnessMen's WellnessMental Well-BeingNutritionParenthoodSexual HealthSkin CareVitamins and SupplementsWomen's WellnessMedicationsPrescription MedicationsBotoxDupixentEyleaGLP-1sRepathaRexultiSkyriziTrintellixUbrelvyVraylarProduct ReviewsProduct ReviewsAt-Home TestingCBDFitnessMen's HealthMental HealthNutritionSleepVitamins and SupplementsWomen's HealthResourcesToolsA1C ExplorerCalorie CalculatorMacronutrient CalculatorPill IdentifierSleep CalculatorEngageBezzy CommunitiesDaily Dose LessonsGLP-1 GuideHealth NewsNewslettersRecipesVideo LibraryJoin our communityFollow Healthline on our socials for all things health.Find a DoctorFindCareCardiologyDentistryDermatologyNeurologyOB-GYNOrthopedic SurgeryPediatricsPrimary CarePsychiatryUrologySearch HealthlineSubscribeBack PainBasicsNavigating CareManaging PainLiving WellProducts Share this article\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.About UsContact UsTerms of UsePrivacy NoticePrivacy SettingsAdvertising PolicyLicensing RequestsHealth TopicsSitemapMedical AffairsContent IntegrityNewslettersYour Privacy Choices\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.AboutCareersAdvertise with usOUR BRANDSHealthlineMedical News TodayGreatistPsych CentralBezzy", "content_hash": "7bb9b326c9736dfbb216e92853723875c6cad308e1273e1f27efecc922a23073", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:10.516693+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1428", "title": "NDIC Celebrates Women's Empowerment at International Women's Day 2026 Observance", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-celebrates-women-s-empowerment-at-international-women-s-day-2026-observance", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=ndic-celebrates-women-s-empowerment-at-international-women-s-day-2026-observance", "text": "NDIC Celebrates Women's Empowerment at International Women's Day 2026 Observance The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) hosted a memorable International Women's Day (IWD) 2026 celebration, bringing together senior management and the female workforce to commemorate the occasion and celebrate women's contributions to institutional excellence. N NDIC April 2, 2026 1 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) hosted a memorable International Women's Day (IWD) 2026 celebration, bringing together senior management and the female workforce to commemorate the occasion and celebrate women's contributions to institutional excellence.Senior management presence was notably strong, with Managing Director/Chief Executive Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, Executive Director Corporate Services Mrs. Emily Osuji, and Executive Director Operations Dr. Kabir Katata in full attendance. Their presence underscored organizational commitment to gender inclusion and women's empowerment initiatives.The event featured distinguished speakers and panelists who educated and motivated the female workforce. The presentations focused on empowering women to embrace the Corporation's core values, recognize opportunities for continuous professional growth, and take active roles in advancing institutional objectives.The IWD 2026 celebration created a platform for recognizing the invaluable contributions of women across all levels of the NDIC. The event highlighted the importance of diversity and inclusion in achieving organizational excellence and delivering on the Corporation's mandate to protect depositors and maintain financial system stability.By commemorating International Women's Day, the NDIC demonstrated commitment to fostering an inclusive workplace where women are encouraged to develop their potential, assume leadership positions, and contribute meaningfully to institutional success.The celebration generated great memories and reinforced organizational values centered on respect, equality, and inclusive growth. Such initiatives are essential for building a high-performing, motivated workforce capable of delivering excellent service to depositors and stakeholders nationwide. All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "52728491f9781144e9b1e57f2609508cdcd21514ec8fe313f024df4bfd0c900e", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:11.141972+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1429", "title": "Patient Journeys and Research Facts in Cancer Care", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/real-experiences-and-key-insights-on-cancer-and-clinical-research#1", "final_url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/video/real-experiences-and-key-insights-on-cancer-and-clinical-research#1", "text": "Patient Journeys and Research Facts in Cancer Care Skip to main contentSubscribeHealth ConditionsHealth ConditionsAlzheimer's DiseaseBreast CancerCancer CareChronic Kidney DiseaseChronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD)Colon CancerDigestive HealthEczemaEye HealthHeart HealthMenopauseMental HealthMigraineMultiple Sclerosis (MS)Parkinson's DiseasePsoriasisRheumatoid Arthritis (RA)Sleep HealthType 2 DiabetesWeight ManagementWellnessWellness TopicsAllergiesCBDFitnessMen's WellnessMental Well-BeingNutritionParenthoodSexual HealthSkin CareVitamins and SupplementsWomen's WellnessMedicationsPrescription MedicationsBotoxDupixentEyleaGLP-1sRepathaRexultiSkyriziTrintellixUbrelvyVraylarProduct ReviewsProduct ReviewsAt-Home TestingCBDFitnessMen's HealthMental HealthNutritionSleepVitamins and SupplementsWomen's HealthResourcesToolsA1C ExplorerCalorie CalculatorMacronutrient CalculatorPill IdentifierSleep CalculatorEngageBezzy CommunitiesDaily Dose LessonsGLP-1 GuideHealth NewsNewslettersRecipesVideo LibraryJoin our communityFollow Healthline on our socials for all things health.Find a DoctorFindCareCardiologyDentistryDermatologyNeurologyOB-GYNOrthopedic SurgeryPediatricsPrimary CarePsychiatryUrologySearch HealthlineSubscribeContent created by Healthline and supported by advertising. Learn more An overview of cancer and clinical trials, blending key facts with real patient stories.Produced by the Healthline Video Team on February 13, 2026\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.About UsContact UsTerms of UsePrivacy NoticePrivacy SettingsAdvertising PolicyLicensing RequestsHealth TopicsSitemapMedical AffairsContent IntegrityNewslettersYour Privacy Choices\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.\u00c2\u00a9 2026 Healthline Media LLC. All rights reserved. Healthline Media is an RVO Health Company. Our website services, content, and products are for informational purposes only. Healthline Media does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. See additional information.AboutCareersAdvertise with usOUR BRANDSHealthlineMedical News TodayGreatistPsych CentralBezzy", "content_hash": "59f32a90cd0ba4137ff152638bdf2b993d038bc16604b635196f8a5c0ac461fe", "domain": "healthline.com", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:13.150144+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1430", "title": "House Commends NDIC On Efficient Budget Implementation", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=house-commends-ndic-on-efficient-budget-implementation", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=house-commends-ndic-on-efficient-budget-implementation", "text": "House Commends NDIC On Efficient Budget Implementation The MD/CE, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday has defended the Corporation\u2019s 2026 budget proposal before the House of Representatives Committee on Insurance & Acturial Matters. N NDIC February 27, 2026 1 min read The MD/CE, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday has defended the Corporation\u2019s 2026 budget proposal before the House of Representatives Committee on Insurance & Acturial Matters. During the session, Mr. Sunday reiterated the commitment of the Corporation to the effective coverage of depositors as well prompt reimbursement in the event of bank failure.The House Committee Chairman, Hon. Ahmadu Jaha commended the Corporation for the effective implementation of its annual budget. Hon Jaha noted that the NDIC has demonstrated strong fiscal discipline in the face of its operation strictly under the cost-to-income ratio, remitting 50 percent of its income to the Consolidated Revenue Fund of Federal Government. Speaking at the session, Hon. Jaha said: \u201cI want to put it on record that NDIC is one of the agencies operating strictly under the Fiscal Responsibility Framework on cost-to-income ratio. 50 percent of of its income must be remitted to a dedicated Consolidated Revenue Fund account, while the remaining 50 percent is retained to run the agency\u201d.He stated that this constraint notwithstanding, NDIC as a self-funding government-owned agency has managed its revenue efficiently within the fiscal responsibility guidelines to be able to meet up with its remittances to the Federal Government. The Committee therefore emphasized its committed to supporting the Corporation to complete its ongoing capital projects without undue delay. All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "1469715fa2d74ab9ac17fd8bd35c0dd75821cd7a6b6700aebdc009ee36cbb1a5", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:13.649400+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1431", "title": "Sale of Assets of Closed Micro Finance Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=sale-of-assets-of-closed-micro-finance-banks-by-public-auction-and-public-competitive-bid", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=sale-of-assets-of-closed-micro-finance-banks-by-public-auction-and-public-competitive-bid", "text": "Sale of Assets of Closed Micro Finance Banks by Public Auction and Public Competitive Bid N NDIC February 11, 2026 4 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), in exercise of its right as Liquidator of failed Micro finance banks (MFBs), hereby invites interested members of the general public to buy the assets (furniture, fixture, fittings, equipment, generators, motor vehicles etc) of the under listed defunct MFBs by PUBLIC COMPETITIVE BIDDING/AUCTION and sealed Bids for Motor Vehicles and Generators:NDIC MICROFINANCE BANK AUCTIONS - FEBRUARY 2026(Auction Dates: 24/02/2026 \u2013 27/02/2026)ABUJAFCT Microfinance Bank, Center For Arts and Culture Area 10, GarkiAuctioneer: Oko Oroma Ventures Ltd (07032682583)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798AKWA IBOMActive Point Microfinance Bank, 150, Oron Road, UyoAuctioneer: Obot Akpan & Co (08023252472)NDIC Contact: PORT HARCOURT ZONAL OFFICE, No. 104, Woji Road, off Olu Obasanjo Road, GRA, Port Harcourt, Rivers State \u2014 08023202134ANAMBRAAguleri Microfinance Bank, 16, Irenso Street, Amaeze, AguleriAuctioneer: Chief J.C.I Ogbuagu & Co (08033368554)NDIC Contact: ENUGU ZONAL OFFICE, No 10, Our Lords' Street, Independence Layout, Enugu \u2014 08035769858Dominion Microfinance Bank, Eke Ihembosi, Ekwusigo LGAAuctioneer: Nonye Ezeagu & Associates (08068405002)NDIC Contact: ENUGU ZONAL OFFICE, No 10, Our Lords' Street, Independence Layout, Enugu \u2014 08035769858Utuh Microfinance Bank, Oye Market Square, Utuh, Nnewi South LGAAuctioneer: Victoria Chidi Akim & Associates (08068910670)NDIC Contact: ENUGU ZONAL OFFICE, No 10, Our Lords' Street, Independence Layout, Enugu \u2014 08035769858CROSS RIVERCalabar Microfinance Bank, 72 Egerton Street, CalabarAuctioneer: Okonuga Nig. Ltd (08028512633 & 08161399124)NDIC Contact: PORT HARCOURT ZONAL OFFICE, No. 104, Woji Road, off Olu Obasanjo Road, GRA, Port Harcourt, Rivers State \u2014 08023202134DELTAIC-Global Microfinance Bank, 312, Effurun/Sapele Road, Effurun-WarriAuctioneer: Humphrey Igberase & Co (08064455503)NDIC Contact: BENIN ZONAL OFFICE, No. 28A & B, Benoni Road, Off Airport Road, GRA, Benin City, Edo State \u2014 08035727023Iyede Microfinance Bank, Town Hall Square, Otor-Iyede, Isoko North LGAAuctioneer: Joe Eziashi & Co (08037204627)NDIC Contact: BENIN ZONAL OFFICE, No. 28A & B, Benoni Road, Off Airport Road, GRA, Benin City, Edo State \u2014 08035727023EDOSmartmicrofinance Bank, 164, Sapele Road, Benin CityAuctioneer: Silva Alele & Associates (08037438529)NDIC Contact: BENIN ZONAL OFFICE, No. 28A & B, Benoni Road, Off Airport Road, GRA, Benin City, Edo State \u2014 08035727023ENUGUIfeanyichukwu Microfinance Bank, 78, Old Okigwe Road, NA Quarters, AgwuAuctioneer: Mechetex International Ltd (08033486551)NDIC Contact: ENUGU ZONAL OFFICE, No 10, Our Lords' Street, Independence Layout, Enugu \u2014 08035769858IMOOgbe-Ahiara Microfinance Bank, Onugot-Hse, Afor Ogbe Market, Ogbe Ahiara, Ahiazu MbaiseAuctioneer: Stan Okeahialam & Co (08037960430)NDIC Contact: ENUGU ZONAL OFFICE, No 10, Our Lords' Street, Independence Layout, Enugu \u2014 08035769858KOGIAkwengwu Microfinance Bank, Idanuha Quarters, Behind Old Police Station, Ogaminana, OkenneAuctioneer: J. I. Ajileye & Co (08033114150)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798Kogi Microfinance Bank, Adankolo Area, Opposite Kogi Transmission Station, Okene-Kaba Road, LokojaAuctioneer: Ekundayo Ayodele & Partners (08033770713)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798LAGOSResort Savings & Loans, 12, Boyle Street, Onikan, LagosAuctioneer: Olasunkanmi Enterprises (08023038692)NDIC Contact: NDIC (ASSET MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT) \u2014 Garba 08062616662, John 08029997846, Aliyu 08062657895NIGERBibajinre Microfinance Bank, Bida-Abuja Road, Badeggi, Kacha Local GovtAuctioneer: M. B. Nuhu & Company (08037250279)NDIC Contact: BEU (ABUJA), Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja \u2014 08038218798OSUNKJL Microfinance Bank, Amazing Grace Plaza, Alekuwodo, Okefia, OsogboAuctioneer: Rapheal Omotola & Co (08061691998)NDIC Contact: NDIC (ASSET MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT) \u2014 Garba 08062616662, John 08029997846, Aliyu 08062657895OYOIfesowapo Microfinance Bank, Saki Road, Idi-Emi, Sepeteri East LGAAuctioneer: Seun Adeyemi & Co (08033599944)NDIC Contact: NDIC (ASSET MANAGEMENT DEPARTMENT) \u2014 Garba 08062616662, John 08029997846, Aliyu 08062657895PLATEAUFadama Farmers Microfinance Bank, C/O Plateau Agricultural Devt. Project, Fadama, 111 Project Office, Dogon Dutse, JosAuctioneer: Phil Nwachukwu & Associates (08034521261 & 08037021106)NDIC Contact: BAUCHI ZONAL OFFICE, No 3, Abdulkadir Ahmed Road, Bauchi \u2014 08034664736RIVERSCosmopolitan Microfinance Bank, Charis Plaza, 141, Olu Obasanjo Road, Port-HarcourtAuctioneer: MN&M Consult (08064669704)NDIC Contact: PORT HARCOURT ZONAL OFFICE, No. 104, Woji Road, off Olu Obasanjo Road, GRA, Port Harcourt, Rivers State \u2014 08023202134AUCTION PROCESSThe Public Auction for the furniture, fixtures, fittings & equipment will take place from 24th to 27th February, 2026.CONDITIONS FOR BIDDING FOR THE GENERATORS AND MOTOR VEHICLES1)Bids should be submitted in a sealed envelope together with a deposit of 10% of the bid price in Certified Bank Draft in favour of the respective microfinance banks (In-Liquidation) and with an inscription \u201cBID FOR GEN SET/MOTOR VEHICLE,\u201d on the top left hand corner of the envelope. The bid should contain the name, address and telephone numbers of the bidder. The successful bidder will be required to pay the balance of the bid price within 24 hours of winning the bid.2)The 10% draft for the unsuccessful bidders would be returned immediately.3)Bids should be submitted to the Auctioneers or NDIC Contact persons within the stated period.4)Submitted bids shall be opened before the bidders at the various locations.5)All Assets are sold as \u201cas is\u201d and \u201cnet of all taxes\u201d.6)All purchased items must be evacuated within 24 hours of purchase.For further enquiries, please contact:Director, Asset Management Department,Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation, Lagos Office,Mamman Kotangora House (9th Floor),23A, Marina,Lagos.Tel No: 08062616662Lagos Office All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "f8067870deb344f6d1b5dc00c966216d263784c7bd47261d7e1996ac00617e2f", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:15.536984+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1432", "title": "NDIC, NIESV Strengthen Partnership on Failed Bank Asset Valuation", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=ndic-niesv-strengthen-partnership-on-failed-bank-asset-valuation", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=ndic-niesv-strengthen-partnership-on-failed-bank-asset-valuation", "text": "NDIC, NIESV Strengthen Partnership on Failed Bank Asset Valuation N NDIC December 2, 2025 2 min read The MD/CE of the NDIC, Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, has called on the Nigerian Institution of Estate Surveyors & Valuers (NIESV) to strengthen strategic collaboration with the Corporation as the NDIC relies on NIESV members for accurate and credible valuation of assets of failed banks, which is critical for effective liquidation and payment of depositors. The MD/CE made the call during a courtesy visit by the President/Chairman of Council of the NIESV, Dr. ESV. Victor Adekunle Alonge, and members of his executive team to the NDIC Head Office, Abuja. The NDIC Chief Executive explained that the Corporation relies on precise and credible valuation reports during the liquidation of failed banks to determine the true worth of assets, which enables their sale at the best possible value. Mr. Sunday further noted that proceeds from the sale of these assets are applied toward the payment of depositors\u2019 balances above the insured amount, making accuracy and professionalism in valuation essential to protecting depositor funds. He emphasized that NIESV\u2019s professionalism therefore contributes directly to financial stability and depositor protection by ensuring transparency, fairness, and value-for-money in the disposal of assets and the recovery process. While calling on the leadership of the Institution to uphold the highest ethical standards and guard against insider abuse, the NDIC Chief Executive added that the Corporation is further strengthening its internal processes, including the development of a comprehensive Asset Management Policy to guide asset identification and documentation, valuation procedures, disposal strategies and transparency and accountability in recoveries. The NDIC Chief Executive emphasized the need for stronger collaboration between both institutions, noting that the Corporation welcomes opportunities for joint training and knowledge exchange between NDIC staff and NIESV professionals, particularly in emerging valuation methodologies, asset management, and sustainable valuation practices. President/Chairman of Council of the NIESV, Dr. ESV. Victor Adekunle Alonge reaffirmed the Institution\u2019s commitment to professionalism and integrity. He explained that NIESV was established by an Act of Parliament and maintains strict disciplinary procedures to sanction any member found to be unethical or unprofessional. He reaffirmed the Institution\u2019s commitment to sustained cooperation and technical support to the NDIC, noting that the partnership remains vital to enhancing service delivery and strengthening public confidence in the banking system. The courtesy visit underscored the shared commitment of both institutions to deepen collaboration, enhance professional standards, and strengthen the bank liquidation process in Nigeria for the overall stability of the financial system. Hawwau GamboHead, Communication & Public Affairs Department All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "80b8800d885194afa44fdd9c03959569f7a9f2ed73ca82e732388a507eccc16b", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:17.812348+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1433", "title": "NOTICE TO GENERAL PUBLIC FOR DISPOSAL OF PHYSICAL ASSETS OF HERITAGE BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION)", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=notice-to-general-public-for-disposal-of-physical-assets-of-heritage-bank-in-liquidation", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=notice-to-general-public-for-disposal-of-physical-assets-of-heritage-bank-in-liquidation", "text": "NOTICE TO GENERAL PUBLIC FOR DISPOSAL OF PHYSICAL ASSETS OF HERITAGE BANK (IN-LIQUIDATION) N NDIC November 3, 2025 4 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), in exercise of its statutory mandate as the Liquidator of failed banks under Section 62(1)(d) of the NDIC Act, 2023 (as amended), hereby invites interested members of the general public to participate in the disposal of the landed properties and physical assets of Heritage Bank Limited (In-Liquidation).The defunct bank\u2019s assets, which are located in fifteen (15) sites across the nation, will be auctioned in phases to ensure broad participation.All interested bidders are invited to note the following:1.Auctions shall be conducted in transparent and competitive manner, with interested bidders required to adhere strictly to the prescribed guidelines.2.The process is open to all reputable individuals, corporate entities and consortia with proven financial capacity.3.The landed properties, which are listed in the following schedule, shall be sold on an \u201cas-is\u201d basis and net of all taxes.4.Each bid must be sealed and accompanied by the following:a.10% of the bid value in bank draft drawn in favour of Heritage Bank (in liquidation), as bid security.b.A letter of introduction from a licensed commercial/merchant or specialized bank, confirming the financial capacity of the bidder or other verifiable proof of funds.c.For corporate bidders, a profile of the company, including the Corporate Affairs Commission registration and 3 years\u2019 tax clearance certificates (if applicable).d.For private individual bidders, the requirements in \u2018a\u2019 and \u2018b\u2019 above suffice.5.Bids without the required 10% bank draft will be rendered invalid.6.Bids can be submitted at the designated NDIC, Zonal Offices or the Corporation\u2019s Asset Management Department (9th Floor), Mamman Kontagora House, 23A Marina, Lagos.7.Successful bidders who fail to make the final payment within the stipulated time frame shall have their bids invalidated and forfeit their 10% bid-security8.All bidders shall be given the opportunity to inspect the properties on specific dates within one (1) week, prior to the scheduled auction date.For properties in Lagos (3) days will be allocated for inspection from 12th to 14th November, 2025, between 10:00 a.m. and 3:30 p.m.For properties outside Lagos Two (2) days will be allocated for inspection from 13th to 14th November, 2025, between 10.00 a.m and 3.30 p.m.Where a property has a sitting tenant or long-term leaseholder, such occupant shall be granted the right of first refusal, subject to meeting the amount of the winning competitive bid.9.All interested bidders and members of the general public are invited to attend the bid-opening sessions at the respective auction centers;a.South-West ZoneFor branches located in Lagos, Oyo, Ogun, Ondo and Ekiti States.Venue: NDIC Lagos Office (Asset Management Department), Mamman Kontagora House, 23A Marina, Lagos.Date: Thursday, 20th November, 2025, 11.00am prompt.b.South-East ZoneFor branches located in Enugu, Anambra and Imo States.Venue: NDIC Enugu Zonal Office, 10 Independence Layout, Enugu.Date: 20th November, 2025, 11.00am prompt.c.South-South ZoneFor branches located in Rivers, Delta, Akwa Ibom, Cross River and Bayelsa States.Venue: NDIC Port Harcourt Zonal Office, 104 Woji Road, off Olu Obasanjo Road, GRA, Port Harcourt.Date: 21st November, 2025, 11.00am prompt. d.North-Central ZoneFor branches located in Kwara State.Venue: NDIC Corporate Head Office, Plot 447/448, Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, Abuja.Date: 21st November, 2025, 11.00am prompt.9.For further inquiries, please contact:Director, Asset Management Department,Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation, Lagos Office Annex,Mamman Kontagora House (9th Floor),23A, Marina,Lagos.Tel No: 08029997846 & 08062616662Tel: 01-2719010; 01-4663400Email: helpdesk@ndic.gov.ngANNEXURE (A)PROPERTY HOLDINGS BY REGIONSOUTH WESTLagos130, Ahmadu Bello Way, Victoria Island (Head Office Annex) \u2014 Multi-storey (high rise) buildingEngineering Close, Victoria Island \u2014 Undeveloped plot of land (2,055.28 sqm)Eredo, Along Ijebu-Ode Road, Epe Area \u2014 BuildingEkitiNo 5, Lane 6, Olujoda Estate, Ikere Road, Ado-Ekiti \u2014 BuildingNORTH CENTRALKwaraNo 4, Ibrahim Malik Close, Old GRA, Ilorin \u2014 Undeveloped plot of land (1,390.42 sqm)SOUTH SOUTHBayelsaNo 104, Mbiama-Yenagoa Road, Yenagoa \u2014 BuildingAkwa-IbomNo. 57, Eket\u2013Oron Road, Eket \u2014 BuildingRivers473A, Trans Amadi Industrial Layout, Port Harcourt \u2014 Undeveloped plot of land (3,476.25 sqm)Cross RiverPlot 6, Northern Industrial Estate, Calabar \u2014 Undeveloped plot of land (4,437.13 sqm)DeltaFormer Midwest Cement Factory, Opposite NPA Koko Village, Warri North LGA \u2014 Bare land and makeshift structuresSOUTH EASTEnuguPlot 32, New Town Layout, Emene \u2014 BuildingPlot 105, New Town Layout, Emene \u2014 BuildingPlot 108, New Town Layout, Emene \u2014 BuildingImo67, Owerri Road, Opposite Abakpa Main Market, Beside Fidelity Bank, Okigwe \u2014 BuildingOriagu Nsu, Opposite the Timber Shade, Along Umuahia/Okigwe/Onitsha Road, Ehieme-Mbano LGA \u2014 BuildingSigned:ManagementNigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "adf4fc8345fc279d27ded6f4160dfafe3b89dced3ae8bd901cc85273beeb5d65", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:19.782813+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1434", "title": "GENERAL PROCUREMENT ACTIVITIES FOR 2025", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=general-procurement-activities-for-2025", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/article?slug=general-procurement-activities-for-2025", "text": "GENERAL PROCUREMENT ACTIVITIES FOR 2025 N NDIC September 1, 2025 1 min read NIGERIA DEPOSIT INSURANCE CORPORATIONPlot 447/448 Constitution Avenue, Central Business District, AbujaE-mail: info@ndic.gov.ng, Website: www.ndic.gov.ngThe Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) wishes to draw the attention of the general public to the notice of General Procurement Activities for 2025 to all interested, competent, reputable contractors/suppliers, consultants and service providers that the Corporation would commence procurement process for Works, Goods and Consultancy Services for all its offices located across the country during the year 2025 as listed below:1.CONSTRUCTION WORKS2.SUPPLY OF OFFICE EQUIPMENT3.SUPPLY OF COMPUTER EQUIPMENT AND OTHER HARDWARE INFRASTRUCTURE4.SUPPLY OF FURNITURE5.VARIABLE REFRIGERANT FLOW AIR CONDITIONING SYSTEM6.PROCUREMENT OF UTILITY VEHICLES7.PROVISION OF FIRE SUPPRESSION SYSTEM8.RENOVATION UPGRADE OF OFFICE BUILDINGSPlease be informed that specific request for tender would be advertised in due course. For enquiries, contact:The Director,Procurement & Management Service Department,Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation,Plot 447/448 Constitution Avenue,Central Business District Abuja, Nigeria. SignedManagement All Articles Share More Articles July 22, 2026 Hon. Minister of Finance's Keynote Speech at IADI-ARC Workshop 2026 July 21, 2026 MD/CE NDIC\u2019S Welcome Remark at IADI-ARC Workshop & Annual Meeting 2026 July 17, 2026 NDIC Hosts IADI Africa Regional Committee Meeting 2026 July 1, 2026 Update on the Revocation of the Operating Licenses of 46 Micro-Finance Banks by the Central Bank of Nigeria June 19, 2026 Disposal of Landed Properties and Other Physical Assets, Defunct Primary Mortgage Banks Browse all articles", "content_hash": "b015462bd7c22d0e12de45f0a11586931e0c91deb8ffba5d1f7a117854dbf063", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:21.588294+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1435", "title": "Notice to Beneficiaries, Allottees and General Public, Housing Estates, Ahocol Savings and Loans Ltd. (In-Liquidation)", "url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=notice-to-beneficiaries-allottees-and-general-public-in-respect-of-some-housing-estates-formerly-acquired-by-ahocol-savings-and-loans-ltd-in-liquidation", "final_url": "https://ndic.gov.ng/news-detail?slug=notice-to-beneficiaries-allottees-and-general-public-in-respect-of-some-housing-estates-formerly-acquired-by-ahocol-savings-and-loans-ltd-in-liquidation", "text": "Notice to Beneficiaries, Allottees and General Public, Housing Estates, Ahocol Savings and Loans Ltd. (In-Liquidation) N NDIC August 26, 2025 1 min read The Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), official liquidator of the defunct AHOCOL SAVINGS AND LOANS LTD. (In-Liquidation), hereby calls on allottees and other interested parties of the following underlisted estates previously acquired by the failed bank and now under the custody of the NDIC as Liquidator, that a verification exercise and physical reconfirmation of Land Allocation will be carried out by NDIC officials on the scheduled dates below. The estates are:1)Legacy Housing Estate (Phase 1, 2 & 3), Mgbakwu \u2013 27th Wednesday, 2025, 2pm \u2013 5pm2)Chukwuemaka Housing Estate (Phase 1 & 2), Mgbakwu \u2013 Thursday 28th August, 2025, 9am-5pm3) Ifeodioranma International Housing Estate (Phase 1 & 2), Mbakwu\u2013 Friday 29th, 2025, 9am \u2013 5pm4)University Campus Estate (Phase 1 & 2), Ukwulu \u2013 9am \u2013 5pm, Friday 29th, 20255)Millennium Housing Estate (Phase 1 & 2), Urum \u2013 9am \u2013 5pm, Saturday, August 30th, 20256)Oriental Housing Estate, Aguilera \u2013 9am-5pm, Saturday, August 30th, 2025VENUE: Emperor Melaine Hotel, Unizik Junction, along Enugu/Onitsha express way, besides Parktonia hotel, Awka, AnambraPlease Note that adherence to the above stated times and dates is mandatory. Allottees are expected to come with documents evidencing purchase, allocation and title in addition to a valid means of Identification.SignedManagementNigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC) All News Share More News October 2, 2026 NDIC Clinches Verbatim\u2019 s Pillar of Integrity in Public Service Award September 30, 2026 Keynote Address by the Managing Director/Chief Executive, Nigeria Deposit Insurance Corporation (NDIC), Mr. Thompson Oludare Sunday, on the Occasion of NDIC\u2019s Special Day at the 21st Abuja International Trade Fair, Wednesday, 30th September 2026 August 14, 2026 NDIC Reinforces Financial Safety Net Role Amid Banking Sector Reforms July 20, 2026 NDIC Hosts International Deposit Insurers' Africa Regional Meeting in Abuja July 7, 2026 SERVICOM Commends NDIC on Efficient Service Deliver to Stakeholders Browse all news", "content_hash": "dec8dfdc9b967bfccb30ab849ad40d373e0e14fe91b00f862f75aeba6a321716", "domain": "ndic.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:23.607127+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1436", "title": "Health A-Z", "url": "https://www.healthline.com/directory/news", "final_url": "https://